=¬ı<”gºıÃÍº™)W<ág;õÒºÛÚü<Cîµ;xy–;”9¢º‰˙º{;Æî~º†.RºqÍq;≈w-=ä‰<Àhºç·πÕs±ºƒÂ—ºÀOz=™ÚDºtD<ºü¡,<H$=µ≠	ΩW.˜;*jñ:(k<eL4Ω«p∫(M=#9=`·å<#§%==␀∂=ºE=¡cºÉ·˙ªAp˛º'FﬂºkI∑<m&<UÇ<üed=≈<ƒÂ—º‘êª∂Hºêﬁ<TQ∫ƒÆ?∫íëì<ç<±\m:™Úƒ<≤J=U¯cªF␀‹ªú˘Ω∫d∫XªÊf>;˜°º≤óº;èÉ<ÌıúªzA?<°â;µ%<Q1tªˆ∫é<„¯;J«Àº¨ù<†˜øºmÏÔ∫;<ÈºÃ™√ªE7ÓºF……<é7…∫qèº∏ÎÀ<¥I;ﬂ3(;"7␀Ω>)é<ﬂaåº¢ˆ¿<{Âˆªk@â=∑µ∏<9tz=J«ÀºXÕºS0ı;—hÖºQÑΩ#9<,iª≠ï}º◊n∂<a ;»¨A;˚à=K˝ﬁªaEΩÓb¬<j‹ëºöçºôƒ)Ωó†rºyØc< ºª∞ÔGΩı(≥ª¬Ê–<ƒ∫7>Áºç¯ªÖ≤<aEÑª¨ù;«vÆºâ˙ÖºWS-<ı(3º_O±;—kºg£ªñèïºSU´ªGí∑<{”Ω#“	<=éÑ<}<KY'<ZàA<™üªï˝πºﬁ4ºoGπ∫)|rªRåΩ<Ãº„’·º4.âºÿ␀=üe‰∫_ü;´_jº∫Fï:≠∫3ºÛ)2ºCîµª¡ˆºˇ#∏ª@(è=¶£º≈w≠∫˛Ä<,÷<ºÔ+∞;U<Ã·U∫|@¿ººE<*j<Â˘òº§Qä<®°;oGπ;ïjﬂ:mµ›º±Å#=˝$∑∫π}ßªÕÈ;fÇ«ª‰√Ö<u;éºÅ–∫‡†Mºò2NΩZøSºVO=7>ÁºóÛå;0‘><—:!ª4“@<ÛÚ=ë»•<Uö∫Î—ÂºáÕ†<º˚º∂H<£à=<ŒDº•ôy:õg‚<lJ=^ÜCªo>ãº£ø.Ω>ÕEº™ÚDºPç<ΩÍõ“<Pç<ΩXÂΩÅ´Áπ≥∑∂;Ø]l=(4ºÑ<DΩ—q3;gÔlºó≈(=*j<O˚`;{"title": "DESMOPRESINA:Desmopresina is a synthetic medication that serves multiple purposes in the medical field. Primarily, it is used in the treatment of diabetes insipidus, especially in its central form, where there is a deficiency of the antidiuretic hormone (ADH). Additionally, Desmopresina plays a role in managing sodium levels, particularly in conjunction with tolvapt\u00e1n, when sodium levels rise too quickly. It is also utilized in the diagnosis and treatment of conditions related to ADH deficiency and is effective in managing hyponatremia. Overall, Desmopresina is a versatile medication that addresses both the symptoms of diabetes insipidus and the complications associated with sodium imbalances."}{"title": "TEST DE LA SED:The test of the sed is a diagnostic procedure used to differentiate types of diabetes ins\u00edpida based on urine concentration responses."}{"title": "HORMONA ANTIDIUR\u00c9TICA:The \"HORMONA ANTIDIUR\u00c9TICA,\" also known as antidiuretic hormone (ADH) or vasopressin, is a crucial hormone that regulates water retention and balance in the body. Its levels can be influenced by various conditions, including adrenal insufficiency. ADH plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of diabetes ins\u00edpida, a condition characterized by excessive thirst and urination due to insufficient levels of this hormone. Additionally, it is involved in the pathophysiology of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), where excessive release of ADH leads to water retention and dilutional hyponatremia.\n\nThe hormone is particularly relevant in the context of patients undergoing nutritional support, as it affects water balance and can influence electrolyte levels, including magnesium. Overall, the \"HORMONA ANTIDIUR\u00c9TICA\" is essential for maintaining homeostasis in the body's water levels and is a key factor in various medical conditions related to fluid regulation."}{"title": "POLIURIA:POLIURIA is a medical condition characterized by excessive urination, which involves the production of abnormally large volumes of dilute urine. This condition can be a symptom of various underlying health issues, most notably uncontrolled diabetes due to high blood sugar levels. Additionally, POLIURIA is often associated with diabetes ins\u00edpida, a specific type of diabetes that affects the body's ability to regulate water balance."}{"title": "POLIDIPSIA:Polydipsia is a condition characterized by excessive thirst, which is commonly observed in individuals experiencing hyperglycemia. This condition typically arises in response to dehydration or elevated blood sugar levels, and it is often associated with diabetes insipidus. In essence, polydipsia occurs as the body attempts to compensate for fluid loss resulting from high blood sugar levels, particularly in diabetic patients."}{"title": "OSMOLARIDAD URINARIA:Urinary osmolarity is a measure of the concentration of solutes in urine, used in the diagnosis of diabetes ins\u00edpida."}{"title": "OSMOLALIDAD PLASM\u00c1TICA:Osmolalidad plasm\u00e1tica refers to the concentration of solutes in the blood plasma, which is crucial for diagnosing various types of hyponatremia. It serves as a measure of the body's electrolyte-water balance and plays a significant role in diagnosing conditions such as diabetes ins\u00edpida."}{"title": "DENSIDAD URINARIA:Urinary density is a measure of urine concentration, which is relevant in the assessment of diabetes ins\u00edpida.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "P\u00c1RAMO FERN\u00c1NDEZ C.:P\u00e1ramo Fern\u00e1ndez C. is the author of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, which contains comprehensive information on diabetes insipida. Additionally, P\u00e1ramo Fern\u00e1ndez C. has contributed a chapter specifically focused on diabetes insipidus within this manual."}{"title": "POLIDIPSIA PRIMARIA:Polidipsia primaria es un trastorno que se caracteriza por la sed excesiva y la ingesta de grandes cantidades de agua. Esta condici\u00f3n puede resultar en una diluci\u00f3n de la orina, lo que implica que el cuerpo est\u00e1 consumiendo m\u00e1s l\u00edquidos de lo que necesita, afectando as\u00ed el equilibrio h\u00eddrico del organismo."}{"title": "DIABETES INS\u00cdPIDA CENTRAL:La diabetes ins\u00edpida central es un tipo de diabetes ins\u00edpida que resulta de la falta de producci\u00f3n de ADH por la hip\u00f3fisis, lo que lleva a una incapacidad para concentrar la orina."}{"title": "DIABETES INS\u00cdPIDA NEFROG\u00c9NICA:La diabetes ins\u00edpida nefrog\u00e9nica es un tipo de diabetes ins\u00edpida que ocurre cuando los ri\u00f1ones no responden adecuadamente a la ADH, resultando en una incapacidad para concentrar la orina."}{"title": "ADH:ADH, or Antidiuretic Hormone, is a nonapeptide hormone synthesized in the hypothalamus that plays a crucial role in regulating water balance and sodium levels in the body. It helps control the amount of water reabsorbed by the kidneys, thereby regulating water retention. ADH is particularly significant in the context of conditions such as hyponatremia and the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), where its levels can be altered. Additionally, the secretion of ADH can be affected in individuals with eating disorders, highlighting its importance in various physiological and pathological states. Overall, ADH is essential for maintaining homeostasis in the body's water balance."}{"title": "MUERTE CEREBRAL:Muerte cerebral refers to a state of irreversible loss of all brain functions, often leading to complications such as diabetes ins\u00edpida neurog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "HIPOFISITIS IGG4:Hipofisitis IgG4 is a rare autoimmune condition affecting the pituitary gland, characterized by inflammation and often presenting with diabetes ins\u00edpida and other symptoms."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD RELACIONADA CON LA IGG4:Enfermedad relacionada con la IgG4 is a systemic autoimmune disease that can manifest with various symptoms, including those affecting the pituitary gland."}{"title": "HIPOGLICEMIA:HIPOGLICEMIA refers to a condition characterized by abnormally low blood sugar levels, known as hypoglycemia. This condition can arise in various medical situations and is particularly noted as a potential complication in patients with pituitary disorders. Hypoglycemia can occur in a range of medical conditions, highlighting its significance in clinical practice."}{"title": "SIADH:The Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone Secretion (SIADH) is a medical condition characterized by the excessive release of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) without an appropriate physiological stimulus. This abnormal secretion leads to water retention in the body, resulting in euvolemic hyponatremia, a condition where sodium levels in the blood become dangerously low despite normal blood volume. SIADH is responsible for approximately 95% of hyponatremia cases in hospitalized patients.\n\nThe condition can manifest in various forms, including ectopic or eutopic secretion, and is often associated with several diseases and conditions that affect the hypothalamic-pituitary axis. It may also occur following pituitary surgery. Management of SIADH is crucial, as it requires careful monitoring and regulation of sodium levels to prevent complications associated with hyponatremia. The syndrome is discussed in medical literature, including the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" highlighting its significance in clinical practice."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA DE FURST:F\u00f3rmula de Furst is a calculation used to assess a patient's ability to excrete free water, guiding fluid restriction in conditions like SIADH."}{"title": "IONES:Iones refer to charged particles that are monitored in patients with diabetes ins\u00edpida and SIADH to manage electrolyte balance."}{"title": "PITUITARIA:Pituitaria refers to the pituitary gland, which is central to the discussion of conditions like hipofisitis and diabetes ins\u00edpida."}{"title": "LAHERA VARGAS M.:Lahera Vargas M. is an author of a chapter in the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n regarding primary hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "VILLABONA C.:Villabona C. is an author of a chapter in the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n regarding the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH)."}{"title": "TOLVAPT\u00c1N:Tolvapt\u00e1n is a medication primarily used to treat hyponatremia, particularly in patients with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). It functions by blocking the action of antidiuretic hormone (ADH) in the kidneys, specifically targeting the V2 receptor, which promotes water excretion and induces aquaresis. This mechanism helps to manage sodium levels in patients by facilitating the elimination of excess water from the body.\n\nTolvapt\u00e1n can be administered in specific dosages, either orally or via nasogastric tube, depending on the patient's nutritional status. It is particularly beneficial for patients experiencing low sodium levels in the blood, including those with heart failure. Overall, tolvapt\u00e1n serves as a selective vasopressin receptor antagonist that effectively addresses euvolemic hyponatremia by promoting water excretion and helping to restore normal sodium levels."}{"title": "T\u00cdA:T\u00eda refers to thiazide diuretics, which are mentioned as part of the treatment for nephrogenic diabetes insipidus."}{"title": "AMILORIDA:Amilorida is a medication mentioned in the treatment of nephrogenic diabetes insipidus."}{"title": "AINE:AINE refers to non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, which are mentioned in the context of treating hyperaldosteronism."}{"title": "FLUOXETINA:Fluoxetina, also known as fluoxetine, is a medication primarily used as an antidepressant. It is prescribed as part of treatment plans for various conditions, including depression and eating disorders. Fluoxetina has been studied for its effectiveness in reducing binge eating and purging behaviors in patients with eating disorders. Additionally, it is noted that fluoxetine can increase appetite in some individuals. However, it is important to be aware that fluoxetine may lead to the development of Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), particularly in older adults."}{"title": "CLORPROPAMIDA:Clorpropamida is a medication that can cause SIADH"}{"title": "CARBAMACEPINA:Carbamacepina, also known as carbamazepine, is an anticonvulsant medication primarily used to manage seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia. In addition to its anticonvulsant properties, carbamazepine can influence the metabolism of thyroid hormones, which requires monitoring of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) levels in patients who are hypothyroid. Furthermore, carbamazepine has been associated with the development of the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), which can impact the duration of treatment. Overall, carbamazepine is a critical medication in seizure management, but it necessitates careful monitoring due to its effects on thyroid function and potential to induce SIADH."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER PULMONAR DE C\u00c9LULAS PEQUE\u00d1AS:Small cell lung cancer is a type of cancer that can cause ectopic production of vasopressin leading to SIADH"}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR OBSTRUCTIVA CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (EPOC), known in Spanish as Enfermedad Pulmonar Obstructiva Cr\u00f3nica, is a progressive lung condition that encompasses diseases such as emphysema and chronic bronchitis. This condition is characterized by obstructed airflow, which leads to difficulties in breathing. EPOC can also be associated with the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH). Additionally, it is a chronic respiratory illness that requires tailored nutritional interventions, as it can lead to malnutrition and other health complications. Overall, EPOC significantly impacts respiratory function and overall health."}{"title": "SUERO HIPERT\u00d3NICO:Hypertonic saline is a treatment used to rapidly increase sodium levels in patients with severe hyponatremia"}{"title": "HIPOFLISIS:"}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD ADDISON:La enfermedad de Addison es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que resulta en insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria, caracterizada por la falta de producci\u00f3n de hormonas por las gl\u00e1ndulas suprarrenales."}{"title": "NEUROSARCOIDOSIS:La neurosarcoidosis es una enfermedad inflamatoria que puede afectar el sistema nervioso central, aunque en este caso se considera menos probable como causa de los s\u00edntomas de la paciente."}{"title": "ANTIEPILEPTICOS:Antiepileptics are medications primarily used to treat epilepsy by controlling seizures. In addition to their primary function, some antiepileptics may interact with weight loss medications. Furthermore, certain antiepileptics can induce the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH), which is a condition that affects water balance in the body. Overall, antiepileptics play a crucial role in managing epilepsy while also having potential interactions and side effects that need to be considered in patient care."}{"title": "QUIMIOTERAPICOS:Los quimioter\u00e1picos son medicamentos utilizados en el tratamiento del c\u00e1ncer, y ciertos tipos pueden causar SIADH."}{"title": "ANTIDIABETICOS:Los antidiab\u00e9ticos son medicamentos utilizados para controlar la diabetes, y algunos de ellos est\u00e1n relacionados con el SIADH."}{"title": "ANALOGOS DE VASOPRESINA:Los an\u00e1logos de vasopresina son medicamentos que imitan la acci\u00f3n de la vasopresina, y algunos pueden estar implicados en el desarrollo del SIADH."}{"title": "CASO CLINICO 1:El caso cl\u00ednico 1 describe una situaci\u00f3n m\u00e9dica espec\u00edfica que involucra a una paciente con s\u00edntomas compatibles con insuficiencia suprarrenal."}{"title": "CORTISOL BAJO:El cortisol bajo es un hallazgo bioqu\u00edmico que indica insuficiencia suprarrenal en la paciente."}{"title": "HIPERPIGMENTACION CUTANEO-MUCOSA:La hiperpigmentaci\u00f3n cut\u00e1neo-mucosa es un signo cl\u00ednico que puede indicar enfermedad de Addison, que es una forma de insuficiencia suprarrenal primaria."}{"title": "TUMORACION HIPOFISARIA:La tumoraci\u00f3n hipofisaria es una posible causa de d\u00e9ficit de ACTH, que puede llevar a insuficiencia suprarrenal secundaria."}{"title": "HIPOFISITIS AUTOINMUNE:La hipofisitis autoinmune es una inflamaci\u00f3n de la hip\u00f3fisis que puede causar d\u00e9ficit de ACTH y otros d\u00e9ficits hormonales."}{"title": "OLIVA GARCIA JG:Oliva Garc\u00eda JG is one of the authors of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, contributing to the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "PEREZ LUIS JM:P\u00e9rez Luis JM is one of the authors of the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, focusing on hormonal functions and treatments."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL SECUNDARIA:Insuficiencia suprarrenal secundaria is a medical condition diagnosed in the patient, indicating a deficiency in adrenal hormone production."}{"title": "HIDROCORTISONA:Hidrocortisona, also known as hydrocortisone, is a corticosteroid medication primarily used to treat adrenal insufficiency and inflammation. It is classified as a glucocorticoid and is commonly prescribed for conditions such as primary adrenal insufficiency, where it serves as a crucial hormone replacement therapy. The typical dosage for patients may vary, with a common prescription being 20 mg per day, depending on the individual's specific health needs and conditions.\n\nIn addition to its role in managing adrenal insufficiency, Hidrocortisona is utilized in the treatment of various hormone deficiencies and can be effective in addressing acute adrenal insufficiency by providing necessary hormone replacement. Furthermore, it has been noted that Hidrocortisona can assist in increasing sodium levels in patients suffering from hyponatremia. Overall, Hidrocortisona is an essential medication in the management of adrenal-related disorders and other conditions requiring corticosteroid therapy."}{"title": "PRUEBA FUNCIONAL:Prueba funcional refers to dynamic functional tests used to evaluate the reserve of the pituitary gland, particularly in assessing hormonal deficiencies."}{"title": "MINERALOCORTICOIDES:Mineralocorticoides son una clase de hormonas esteroides que desempe\u00f1an un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n del equilibrio de electrolitos en el cuerpo, espec\u00edficamente en la regulaci\u00f3n de los niveles de sodio y potasio. Estas hormonas, que se producen principalmente en la zona glomerulosa de la corteza adrenal, influyen en la presi\u00f3n arterial y el balance de fluidos. Adem\u00e1s, los mineralocorticoides pueden afectar la excreci\u00f3n de magnesio, lo que resalta su importancia en la homeostasis electrol\u00edtica general."}{"title": "DEXAMETASONA:DEXAMETASONA, also known as dexamethasone, is a synthetic glucocorticoid and corticosteroid medication utilized in various medical contexts. It is commonly employed in the suppression test to evaluate autonomous cortisol secretion in patients with adrenal incidentalomas. Dexametasona is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. In the context of chemotherapy, it has been shown to improve patients' general condition and assist in managing pharmacological evening hyperglycemia. Additionally, dexamethasone is recognized for its ability to reduce inflammation and suppress the immune response, thereby enhancing the quality of life and alleviating asthenia in cancer patients."}{"title": "CRISIS DE AUSENCIA:Crisis de ausencia refers to a type of seizure characterized by brief lapses in consciousness. Individuals experiencing this condition typically have a history of such episodes."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO:Deficit de hormona de crecimiento refers to the condition diagnosed in the patient, indicating a lack of growth hormone production."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N DE RESERVA FUNCIONAL SOMATOTROPA:Evaluaci\u00f3n de reserva funcional somatotropa is a clinical assessment process to evaluate the function of the growth hormone axis in patients."}{"title": "GH TRAS GLUCAG\u00d3N:GH tras glucag\u00f3n refers to a specific test used to evaluate growth hormone levels in patients, particularly after administration of glucagon."}{"title": "HIPOGLICEMIA INSUL\u00cdNICA:Hipoglucemia insul\u00ednica is a test used to stimulate growth hormone release by inducing low blood sugar levels."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD A LARGO PLAZO:Mortalidad a largo plazo refers to the long-term mortality risk that may be addressed through treatment of growth hormone deficiency."}{"title": "NEURONT\u00cdN:"}{"title": "\u00d3SCAR MORENO P\u00c9REZ:\u00d3scar Moreno P\u00e9rez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, coordinator of the Diabetes Unit at the General University Hospital of Alicante, and associated professor at the Miguel Hern\u00e1ndez University."}{"title": "REBECA REYES GARC\u00cdA:Rebeca Reyes Garc\u00eda is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, a doctor in Medicine and Surgery from the University of Granada, and a member of the Diabetes Working Group of the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "CL\u00cdNICA SAN PEDRO:San Pedro Clinic is a medical facility in Almer\u00eda where Rebeca Reyes Garc\u00eda also works in the Endocrinology Service."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD MIGUEL HERN\u00c1NDEZ:Miguel Hern\u00e1ndez University is an educational institution where \u00d3scar Moreno P\u00e9rez serves as an associate professor in the Clinical Medicine Department."}{"title": "INSTITUTO DE INVESTIGACI\u00d3N SANITARIA Y BIOM\u00c9DICA DE ALICANTE:The Alicante Health and Biomedical Research Institute (ISABIAL) is where \u00d3scar Moreno P\u00e9rez coordinates research on diabetes and associated metabolic diseases."}{"title": "TYPE 1 DIABETES:Type 1 Diabetes is a form of diabetes that typically develops in children and young adults. It is classified as an autoimmune condition, characterized by the destruction of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas. This destruction leads to high blood sugar levels, as the body is unable to produce insulin. Consequently, individuals with Type 1 Diabetes require lifelong management through insulin therapy to regulate their blood sugar levels effectively."}{"title": "DR3-DQ2:DR3-DQ2 is a haplotype associated with increased susceptibility to Type 1 Diabetes, significantly raising the relative risk of developing the disease."}{"title": "DR4-DQ8:DR4-DQ8 is another haplotype that confers a higher risk of developing Type 1 Diabetes, contributing to the genetic predisposition to the disease."}{"title": "ATKINSON MA:Atkinson MA is a researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding of Type 1 Diabetes, particularly in relation to its genetic factors. His work has advanced the knowledge surrounding this autoimmune condition, helping to elucidate the underlying mechanisms that contribute to its development."}{"title": "EISENBARTH GS:Eisenbarth GS is a prominent figure and scientist in the field of diabetes research, with a particular focus on type 1 diabetes. His contributions to the understanding and treatment of this condition have established him as a key player in the scientific community dedicated to diabetes research."}{"title": "MICHELS AW:Michels AW is a researcher recognized for his contributions to the field of type 1 diabetes, particularly focusing on its genetic factors and pathogenesis. He has published significant work that explores the underlying mechanisms of the disease, enhancing the understanding of its development and potential treatment avenues."}{"title": "BARRIO CASTELLANOS R:Barrio Castellanos R is an author who has updated knowledge on Type 1 Diabetes in pediatric age."}{"title": "DIABETES 2:Diabetes 2, also known as Type 2 Diabetes, is a chronic condition that significantly impacts the body's ability to process blood sugar (glucose). It is characterized by high blood sugar levels resulting from insulin resistance or insufficient insulin production. This condition can lead to various metabolic complications, including diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic crises, which may necessitate medical interventions such as insulin administration and fluid therapy. Additionally, Diabetes 2 may require insulin treatment and is associated with complications related to the disease. The condition also encompasses discussions on genetic susceptibility and haplotypes that are relevant to Type 1 Diabetes, highlighting the complex interplay of genetic factors in diabetes management."}{"title": "DRB1*1501/DQA1*0102/DQB1*0602:This haplotype is known to confer protection against the development of Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "DRB1*1401/DQA1*0101/DQB1*0503:This haplotype also provides protective effects against Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "DRB1*0701/DQA1*0201/DQB1*0303:This haplotype is associated with a protective effect against Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "DRB1*0405/DQA1*0301/DQB1*0302:This haplotype is one of the most susceptible to Type 1 Diabetes, indicating a high risk of developing the disease."}{"title": "DRB1*0401/DQA1*0301/DQB1*0302:This haplotype is also linked to a higher susceptibility to Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "DRB1*0402/DQA1*0301/DQB1*0302:This haplotype is associated with increased risk for Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "DRB1*0404/DQA1*0301/DQB1*0302:This haplotype has a moderate association with susceptibility to Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "DRB1*0801/DQB1*0401/DQB1*0402:This haplotype is also linked to susceptibility to Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "GLUCAGON:GLUCAGON is a hormone produced by the alpha cells in the pancreatic islets of the pancreas. Its primary function is to elevate blood glucose levels, which it achieves by promoting gluconeogenesis and glycogenolysis, processes that convert glycogen into glucose. This hormone plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism and acts as a counter-regulatory hormone to insulin, particularly important in the context of hypoglycemia. Additionally, glucagon's release can be suppressed during hypoglycemic episodes. It is also noted for its potential role in regulating metabolism during parenteral nutrition and is particularly relevant in the management of Type 1 Diabetes and glycogen storage diseases."}{"title": "AUMENTO DE LA HIGIENE:Increased hygiene has been associated with a higher incidence of Type 1 Diabetes, suggesting a link between environmental factors and the disease."}{"title": "HERMANOS:Siblings sharing HLA haplotypes have a different risk of developing Type 1 Diabetes, indicating genetic predisposition."}{"title": "GEMELOS MONOCIGOTICOS:Monozygotic twins have a significantly higher risk of developing Type 1 Diabetes if one twin is affected, highlighting genetic factors."}{"title": "HAPLOTIPO HLADR2:Haplotype HLADR2 is known to confer protection against the development of Type 1 Diabetes."}{"title": "FAMILIAS CAUCASICAS:Caucasian families were part of the genetic analysis conducted by the Type 1 Diabetes Genetics Consortium to study the disease."}{"title": "FAMILIAS ASIATICAS:Asian families were also included in the genetic analysis to understand the genetic factors associated with Type 1 Diabetes.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "TYPE 1 DIABETES GENETICS CONSORTIUM:The Type 1 Diabetes Genetics Consortium is a group focused on studying the genetic factors associated with type 1 diabetes risk."}{"title": "HLA DR-DQ HAPLOTYPES:HLA DR-DQ haplotypes are genetic variations that have been studied for their association with type 1 diabetes risk."}{"title": "AIRE GENE:The AIRE gene is associated with autoimmune conditions, including type 1 diabetes, and is involved in immune tolerance."}{"title": "FOXP3 GENE:The FOXP3 gene is crucial for the development of regulatory T cells and is linked to autoimmune diabetes."}{"title": "POLYENDOCRINOPAT\u00cdA AUTOINMUNE DE TIPO 1:Polyendocrinopathy autoimmune type 1 (APECED) is a syndrome caused by a mutation in the AIRE gene, leading to multiple autoimmune conditions including diabetes."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 1:Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 (DM1) is a chronic autoimmune condition characterized by the destruction of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, leading to little or no insulin production. This condition requires continuous and careful management of insulin and dietary intake to maintain healthy blood glucose levels. Patients with DM1 often face challenges related to poor glycemic control, which can complicate their overall health management. \n\nAdditionally, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1 is associated with a higher risk of developing eating disorders, particularly in young women. It frequently coexists with other autoimmune conditions, such as thyroid diseases and celiac disease. The patient has been managing this condition for 6 years, highlighting the long-term commitment required to effectively control the disease and mitigate its associated risks."}{"title": "CROMOSOMA 6P21:Chromosome 6p21 is the location of the major susceptibility locus for type 1 diabetes, containing genes related to the immune response."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 2:Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 (DM2) is a chronic condition characterized by insulin resistance and high blood sugar levels. It primarily affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and is often associated with obesity and other risk factors. This form of diabetes typically develops in adults and is marked by relative insulin deficiency. Management of Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 often involves lifestyle changes, including exercise and diet, and may also require medication. The condition is commonly linked to obesity, highlighting the importance of weight management in its prevention and treatment."}{"title": "GLUCEMIA PLASM\u00c1TICA:GLUCEMIA PLASM\u00c1TICA refers to the measurement of glucose levels in the blood, specifically in the plasma. This measurement is crucial for diagnosing conditions such as diabetes and prediabetes. Additionally, glucemia plasm\u00e1tica is utilized to evaluate carbohydrate metabolism, providing important insights into an individual's metabolic health."}{"title": "PREDIABETES:Prediabetes is a condition characterized by blood sugar levels that are elevated beyond the normal range but not sufficiently high to be classified as diabetes. This condition signifies an increased risk for developing type 2 diabetes (DM2). In the case of Mar\u00eda, her glucose levels indicated that she may have prediabetes, suggesting that she is at a heightened risk for progressing to diabetes if lifestyle changes are not implemented."}{"title": "HBA1C:HbA1c is a blood test that measures average blood sugar levels over the past 2 to 3 months, making it a crucial tool for managing and monitoring diabetes. It provides insights into a patient's glycemic control, with values consistently above 8.5% indicating poor management of blood glucose levels. Throughout treatment, HbA1c levels are monitored to assess the effectiveness of diabetes management strategies. In the context of the BLOOM-DM study, HbA1c serves as an important measure for evaluating diabetes control. The latest analytical results for a patient indicated an HbA1c level of 6.2%, suggesting good control of their diabetes. Overall, HbA1c is essential for both the diagnosis and ongoing management of diabetes, helping healthcare providers tailor treatment plans effectively."}{"title": "LATINOS:Latinos are an ethnic group identified as having a higher risk for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2."}{"title": "AMERICANOS DE ORIGEN ASI\u00c1TICO:Americans of Asian descent are classified as an ethnic group at high risk for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2."}{"title": "ISLAS DEL PAC\u00cdFICO:Pacific Islanders are recognized as an ethnic group with a higher risk for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2."}{"title": "HISTORIA PREVIA DE ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR:A history of cardiovascular disease is a recognized risk factor for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2."}{"title": "HIPERTENSI\u00d3N ARTERIAL:Hipertensi\u00f3n Arterial, or high blood pressure, is a medical condition characterized by a systolic blood pressure (PAS) of 140 mmHg or higher, or a diastolic blood pressure (PAD) of 90 mmHg or higher. It is a chronic condition that can develop due to poor nutrition and lifestyle choices, particularly in children. The condition is associated with elevated blood pressure levels, which can be influenced by sodium intake and is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular diseases.\n\nManagement of Hipertensi\u00f3n Arterial often involves dietary controls, particularly regarding sodium and potassium consumption. It is also recognized as a risk factor for chronic kidney disease and can complicate the management of phosphorus levels. Furthermore, hypertension is linked to the development of Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 and is often addressed through dietary interventions aimed at reducing cardiovascular risk.\n\nWhile some studies have explored the relationship between fish consumption and the incidence of hypertension, findings have been contradictory, indicating that more research is needed to clarify this association. Overall, Hipertensi\u00f3n Arterial is a critical health concern that requires attention to diet and lifestyle to mitigate its risks and complications."}{"title": "DISLIPIDEMIA:Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal levels of lipids in the blood. This condition can manifest in various forms, including mild cases in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0) and more pronounced forms such as hypertriglyceridemia in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII). Dyslipidemia is commonly observed in individuals undergoing dietary treatment and is influenced by diet and lifestyle choices.\n\nThe condition is significant as it increases the risk of cardiovascular diseases, which are responsible for millions of deaths annually. Dyslipidemia is often associated with obesity and is prevalent among patients with diabetes, contributing to the overall risk of developing cardiovascular disease and Diabetes Mellitus Type 2. Effective management of dyslipidemia typically requires tailored dietary interventions and treatment strategies aimed at controlling cholesterol levels to mitigate these health risks."}{"title": "SEDENTARISMO:Sedentarismo, or physical inactivity, is identified as a significant risk factor for various health issues, including cardiovascular disease and the development of Diabetes Mellitus Type 2. To mitigate these risks, regular physical activity is strongly recommended. Engaging in consistent exercise can help counteract the negative effects associated with a sedentary lifestyle, promoting overall health and well-being."}{"title": "HISTORIA PREVIA DE DIABETES GESTACIONAL:A previous history of gestational diabetes is a significant risk factor for developing Diabetes Mellitus Type 2."}{"title": "AFROAMERICANOS:Afroamericans are a demographic group characterized by a higher prevalence of hypertension, which occurs more frequently and at an earlier age compared to Caucasians. Additionally, they have a lower prevalence of hereditary fructose intolerance, with an estimated occurrence of 1 in 200,000 individuals."}{"title": "MODY:MODY (Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young) is a form of diabetes caused by genetic mutations affecting insulin production, characterized by different subtypes with varying clinical features and treatments."}{"title": "HAPO:HAPO (Hyperglycemia and Adverse Pregnancy Outcomes) is a study that established criteria for diagnosing gestational diabetes based on glucose levels during an oral glucose tolerance test."}{"title": "LINAGLIPTINA:Linagliptina is a medication specifically designed for the treatment of type 2 diabetes. It functions by increasing insulin production and decreasing glucose production in the liver, thereby helping to manage blood sugar levels effectively. Notably, Linagliptina does not require dose adjustment in patients with severe renal impairment, making it a suitable option for individuals with compromised kidney function."}{"title": "SULFONILUREAS:Sulfonylureas are a class of medications that serve dual purposes in diabetes management. They are primarily used to treat Type 2 diabetes by stimulating insulin release from the pancreas, thereby helping to lower blood sugar levels. Additionally, sulfonylureas are also utilized in the treatment of certain cases of neonatal diabetes, where they target ATP-dependent potassium channels to regulate insulin secretion. This versatility makes sulfonylureas an important option in the pharmacological management of diabetes across different age groups and types of the disease."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS DE EMPRESA:Company analysis refers to the evaluation of blood glucose levels and other health metrics to diagnose diabetes or prediabetes."}{"title": "CURVA CON 75 G DE GLUCEMIA:The 75g glucose curve test is a diagnostic procedure used to confirm diabetes by measuring blood glucose levels at intervals after consuming a glucose solution."}{"title": "DIABETES GESTACIONAL:Diabetes gestacional is a specific type of diabetes that develops during pregnancy, typically characterized by elevated blood sugar levels. This condition necessitates careful monitoring and management to safeguard the health of both the mother and the baby. Diagnosis usually involves specific screening conducted between the 24th and 28th weeks of gestation. Women with obesity are particularly at risk for developing gestational diabetes. Overall, effective management is crucial to mitigate potential complications associated with this condition."}{"title": "HNF-4\u0391:HNF-4\u03b1 (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 4 Alpha) is a gene associated with MODY type 1, which affects insulin secretion."}{"title": "GLUCOKINASE:Glucokinase is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism, particularly within the \u03b2-cells of the pancreas, where it stimulates insulin secretion. Additionally, glucokinase is associated with maturity onset diabetes of the young (MODY) type 2, highlighting its importance in both normal metabolic processes and in certain genetic forms of diabetes."}{"title": "HNF-1\u0392:HNF-1\u03b2 (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 1 Beta) is a gene that plays a significant role in the development of MODY type 5 (Maturity Onset Diabetes of the Young type 5). This genetic condition is associated with complications affecting both the kidneys and the pancreas. HNF-1\u03b2 is particularly important in the regulation and secretion of insulin, which is crucial for maintaining normal glucose levels in the body. Thus, mutations or dysfunctions in the HNF-1\u03b2 gene can lead to diabetes and related health issues."}{"title": "HNF-1\u0391:HNF-1\u03b1 (Hepatocyte Nuclear Factor 1 Alpha) is a gene associated with MODY type 3, which is linked to microvascular complications."}{"title": "IPF-1:IPF-1 (Insulin Promoter Factor 1) is a gene associated with MODY type 4, which can lead to pancreatic agenesis."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO 2:Diabetes tipo 2 is a chronic medical condition that has affected the patient for 12 years, primarily associated with obesity and challenges in glucose control. This condition significantly impacts how the body processes blood sugar (glucose) and is characterized by insulin resistance and elevated blood sugar levels. It is often linked to various lifestyle factors, including dietary habits such as the consumption of sugary beverages and trans fats, as well as the intake of fiber and whole grains, which may help reduce the risk of developing the disease.\n\nDiabetes tipo 2 is prevalent in Spain and poses a considerable burden on healthcare resources and costs. It is also associated with an increased risk of complications, including cardiovascular disease and uric acid stone formation. The condition can be treated with medications such as liraglutide and may require insulin in some cases. Additionally, diabetes tipo 2 is related to metabolic syndrome and has shown an inverse association with vitamin D levels.\n\nThe rising prevalence of diabetes tipo 2, particularly among older populations, highlights the importance of addressing lifestyle factors and dietary choices to manage and potentially prevent this condition. Furthermore, it is considered in the context of metabolic surgery for obese patients and is often discussed in relation to low-carbohydrate diets and very low-calorie diets (VLCD). Overall, diabetes tipo 2 is a complex metabolic disorder that necessitates a comprehensive approach to treatment and management."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS:AN\u00c1LISIS refers to a comprehensive medical evaluation process that encompasses various assessments related to health metrics. This includes the analysis of blood glucose levels and other health indicators to diagnose conditions such as diabetes or prediabetes. Additionally, AN\u00c1LISIS involves conducting medical tests to evaluate hormone levels and other physiological parameters, particularly in the context of precocious puberty. Furthermore, it encompasses the analytical monitoring of patients with chronic diseases, which is recommended to be performed annually or as clinically indicated. Overall, AN\u00c1LISIS plays a crucial role in the diagnosis and management of various health conditions through systematic evaluations."}{"title": "CIRCUITO DE GLUCOSA:The glucose circuit refers to the metabolic pathway through which glucose is processed in the body, crucial for understanding diabetes management."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES MICROVASCULARES:Microvascular complications are health issues that arise from damage to small blood vessels, commonly associated with poorly managed diabetes."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO:The term \"TRATAMIENTO\" encompasses a variety of medical interventions aimed at improving patient health across different conditions. In the case of classical galactosemia, treatment involves the strict elimination of galactose from the diet starting from the first days of life. For oncology patients, treatment may include a combination of radiotherapy, chemotherapy, and surgery, all of which can significantly impact nutritional status. Additionally, treatment for allergies and food intolerances often requires the removal of specific foods from the diet and the management of associated symptoms. \n\nFurthermore, treatment is a broad term that refers to the medical care provided to patients, which necessitates informed consent. It also includes various methods to manage and alleviate symptoms of inflammatory bowel disease, as well as medical interventions for conditions such as hyponatremia. In the context of diabetes management, treatment involves lifestyle modifications, medications, and insulin therapy. Overall, \"TRATAMIENTO\" signifies a comprehensive approach to healthcare that addresses a wide range of medical conditions through tailored interventions."}{"title": "DIABETES MODY 1:Diabetes MODY 1 is a form of monogenic diabetes that is not usually associated with macrovascular complications but has an increased risk of microvascular complications."}{"title": "DIABETES MODY 2:Diabetes MODY 2 is characterized by mild and stable hyperglycemia, often manageable with diet, and typically does not present symptoms of hyperglycemia."}{"title": "DIABETES MODY 3:Diabetes MODY 3 is characterized by a progressive secretory defect, typically presenting hyperglycemia in childhood or adolescence, and may require insulin treatment as the defect progresses."}{"title": "DIABETES MODY 5:Diabetes MODY 5 can be associated with renal dysplasia, cysts, and renal failure, and may require insulin treatment."}{"title": "SULFONYLUREAS:Sulfonylureas are a class of oral medications primarily used in the treatment of Type 2 diabetes. They function by stimulating insulin secretion from the pancreatic beta cells, thereby increasing insulin production from the pancreas. This mechanism helps to manage blood sugar levels in individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "INSULIN:Insulin is a vital hormone produced by the pancreas that plays a crucial role in regulating glucose levels in the blood. It is primarily used in the treatment of diabetes, particularly for managing blood glucose levels and addressing hyperglycemic crises. Insulin lowers blood sugar levels and is essential for glucose metabolism, as well as the metabolism of carbohydrates, fats, and proteins.\n\nIn diabetes management, insulin is often administered to maintain glycemic control, especially in cases of severe hyperglycemia or progressive secretory defects. The dosage and administration of insulin are typically adjusted based on the individual patient's needs. Additionally, it is important to note that insulin's hypoglycemic effects can be potentiated by alcohol consumption.\n\nIn specific populations, such as patients with Anorexia Nervosa, insulin levels may be appropriately low, and their sensitivity to insulin remains normal. Furthermore, insulin may be administered as necessary during dietary management for patients with various metabolic disorders. Overall, insulin is a critical component in the effective management of diabetes and related metabolic conditions."}{"title": "RENAL DYSPLASIA:Renal dysplasia is a developmental disorder of the kidneys that can be associated with diabetes MODY 5, leading to complications such as renal failure."}{"title": "KCNJ11:KCNJ11 is a gene that encodes a potassium channel that plays a crucial role in the regulation of insulin secretion. Mutations in this gene can lead to conditions such as hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia and neonatal diabetes. Additionally, KCNJ11 is associated with various types of diabetes, particularly those that involve the functioning of potassium channels."}{"title": "ABCC8:ABCC8 is a gene that encodes a protein crucial for the regulation of insulin secretion. It is associated with various types of diabetes, particularly those that affect ATP-sensitive potassium channels. Specifically, ABCC8 encodes a subunit of these channels, and mutations in this gene can lead to conditions such as neonatal diabetes and hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO MODY:Diabetes tipo MODY is a genetic form of diabetes characterized by specific mutations affecting insulin production and secretion, often presenting in childhood or early adulthood."}{"title": "NEUROD1:NEUROD1 is a gene associated with MODY 6 diabetes, playing a role in pancreatic beta-cell function."}{"title": "IPF1:IPF1 is a gene that encodes a transcription factor important for insulin production, associated with MODY 4 diabetes."}{"title": "ZNT8:ZnT8 is a gene that encodes a zinc transporter involved in insulin secretion, associated with diabetes."}{"title": "HIPERINSULINEMIA:Hiperinsulinemia is a condition characterized by excess insulin in the blood, often associated with certain genetic mutations."}{"title": "DIABETES NEONATAL:"}{"title": "O'RIORDAN SM:O'Riordan SM is an author who contributed to the management of cystic fibrosis-related diabetes in children and adolescents."}{"title": "ROBINSON PD:Robinson PD is an author who contributed to the management of cystic fibrosis-related diabetes in children and adolescents."}{"title": "DONAGHUE KC:Donaghue KC is an author who contributed to the management of cystic fibrosis-related diabetes in children and adolescents."}{"title": "MORAN A:Moran A is an author who contributed to the management of cystic fibrosis-related diabetes in children and adolescents."}{"title": "LIPODISTROFIA GENERALIZADA CONGENITA:Lipodystrophy is a genetic disorder characterized by the absence of adipose tissue and is associated with insulin resistance and diabetes."}{"title": "LEPRECHAUNISMO:Leprechaunism is a congenital syndrome characterized by extreme insulin resistance and severe growth retardation due to mutations in the insulin receptor gene."}{"title": "SINDROME DE RABSON-MENDENHALL:Rabson-Mendenhall syndrome is a pediatric syndrome characterized by severe insulin resistance and growth impairment, caused by mutations in the insulin receptor gene."}{"title": "SINDROME DE LA PERSONA RIGIDA:Stiff-person syndrome is a rare neurological disorder characterized by muscle rigidity and spasms, with a notable association with diabetes in some patients."}{"title": "SINDROME DE WOLFRAM:Wolfram syndrome is an autosomal recessive disorder associated with diabetes and other neurological symptoms."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS ANTI-GAD:Anti-GAD antibodies are markers often found in patients with autoimmune diabetes, including those with stiff-person syndrome."}{"title": "LIPODISTROFIA CONG\u00c9NITA GENERALIZADA:Lipodistrofia cong\u00e9nita generalizada is a rare hereditary disorder characterized by the near-total absence of adipose tissue from birth, leading to metabolic anomalies such as hypertriglyceridemia and insulin resistance."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE WOLFRAM:Wolfram syndrome, also known as DIDMOAD, is a rare neurodegenerative disorder characterized by diabetes mellitus type 1, diabetes insipidus, and optic atrophy, caused by mutations in specific genes."}{"title": "SAMUEL NAMARA:Samuel Namara is a multifaceted individual recognized for his contributions in both the medical and business fields. He is primarily a researcher and educator specializing in endocrinology, with a focus on diabetes and nutrition. In addition to his work in endocrinology, he has also engaged in research concerning cardiovascular health and the impact of dietary factors. His involvement extends to studies on dietary fiber and its health outcomes, highlighting his commitment to understanding the relationship between diet and health.\n\nWhile there is a fictional aspect to the name Samuel Namara, including references to a character in a hostage scenario and a hypothetical child with precocious puberty, these elements are not pertinent to his professional contributions. Instead, the emphasis remains on his significant role in dietary studies and his influence in the fields of endocrinology and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2:Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 (DM2) is a prevalent and chronic metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance and relative insulin deficiency, significantly affecting how the body processes blood sugar (glucose). It is particularly common in Spain, with a prevalence rate of 13.8% in the general population and an incidence of 11.58 cases per 1,000 people per year. The condition is often associated with obesity, lifestyle factors, and can lead to serious health complications, including cardiovascular disease and diabetic retinopathy.\n\nPatients with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 may experience varying degrees of control over their condition; some have managed it effectively for many years, while others may face challenges, particularly if it is insulin-dependent and poorly controlled. The condition has been linked to the use of statins, especially in individuals with pre-existing risk factors, indicating a complex relationship between medication and diabetes management.\n\nDiabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is also recognized as a comorbidity that can significantly improve following interventions such as bariatric surgery. Dietary habits and lifestyle choices play a crucial role in managing the disease, with evidence suggesting that adherence to a Mediterranean diet may help prevent its onset. Additionally, the condition has familial links, as indicated by a family history of diabetes in some patients.\n\nOverall, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a significant health issue that requires ongoing management and intervention to mitigate its risks and complications."}{"title": "INSULIN RESISTANCE:Insulin resistance is a condition characterized by the body's cells becoming less responsive to insulin, which can lead to elevated blood glucose levels. This condition is often associated with various metabolic disorders, including type 2 diabetes and metabolic syndrome. Insulin resistance is frequently observed in individuals with obesity and is linked to cardiovascular disease. Additionally, it is commonly seen in patients with Klinefelter syndrome and Polycystic Ovary Syndrome, both of which contribute to the development of metabolic syndrome. Insulin resistance can also occur in critically ill patients, highlighting its relevance across different health contexts. Overall, insulin resistance plays a significant role in the pathophysiology of several metabolic conditions and is influenced by dietary factors and other health-related issues."}{"title": "GLUCONEOGENESIS:Gluconeogenesis is a vital metabolic pathway that generates glucose from non-carbohydrate substrates. This process primarily occurs in the liver, with additional activity in the kidneys and intestines. It plays a crucial role in maintaining blood sugar levels, especially during fasting or periods of low carbohydrate intake. Gluconeogenesis is particularly significant in the context of glycogen storage diseases, such as Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI), and is also affected by specific deficiencies, such as fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency. Furthermore, the process is heightened in critically ill patients, underscoring its importance in metabolic regulation during stress. Overall, gluconeogenesis is an anabolic pathway essential for synthesizing glucose from non-carbohydrate precursors, ensuring energy availability in various physiological states."}{"title": "LIP\u00d3LISIS:LIP\u00d3LISIS es el proceso metab\u00f3lico mediante el cual se descomponen las grasas en el cuerpo, transformando los triglic\u00e9ridos en \u00e1cidos grasos libres y glicerol, que pueden ser utilizados como fuente de energ\u00eda. Este proceso puede verse alterado en diversas condiciones de salud, como en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, donde contribuye a la p\u00e9rdida de peso, o en trastornos como la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada. Adem\u00e1s, la lip\u00f3lisis tiende a aumentar en pacientes cr\u00edticamente enfermos, lo que indica su importancia en situaciones de estr\u00e9s metab\u00f3lico. La regulaci\u00f3n de la lip\u00f3lisis tambi\u00e9n est\u00e1 influenciada por los niveles de insulina, lo que resalta su papel en el metabolismo energ\u00e9tico. En el contexto del embarazo, la lip\u00f3lisis se convierte en una fuente de energ\u00eda crucial para la madre."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTESIS PROTEICA:Protein synthesis is the process by which cells build proteins, essential for growth and repair, and is regulated by insulin among other factors."}{"title": "GLUT2:GLUT2 is a glucose transporter protein that plays a crucial role in the transport of glucose into cells. It is particularly important in the entry of glucose into \u03b2-cells, which is essential for the secretion of insulin. Additionally, GLUT2 is involved in the absorption of glucose and fructose in the intestines, highlighting its significance in both glucose metabolism and dietary sugar absorption."}{"title": "M\u00daSCULO:M\u00daSCULO refers to muscle tissue, a specialized type of tissue in the body that plays a crucial role in movement and strength. It utilizes glycogen as a primary energy source for muscle contraction and is involved in the storage and utilization of glycogen during physical activity. Muscle tissue contains approximately 20% of the total body magnesium, which is essential for various physiological functions. Additionally, it plays a significant role in glucose uptake and metabolism; however, its function can be impaired in cases of insulin resistance, leading to an increase in lipid content.\n\nThe development and performance of muscle tissue are influenced by factors such as exercise and protein intake, with muscle being created through protein synthesis. During stress situations, muscle tissue also releases glutamine, which serves as a key source of this important amino acid. Overall, proper nutrition and training are vital for enhancing the performance of muscle tissue, ensuring its optimal function in the body."}{"title": "CORAZ\u00d3N:The entity \"CORAZ\u00d3N,\" which translates to \"heart,\" is a vital organ that plays a crucial role in the cardiovascular system. It can be significantly impacted by iron overload, which may lead to various cardiovascular issues. Additionally, the heart is also affected by insulin resistance, a condition that can result in alterations in lipid metabolism. These factors highlight the heart's susceptibility to metabolic disturbances and the importance of maintaining overall health to prevent cardiovascular complications."}{"title": "RI\u00d1\u00d3N:Ri\u00f1\u00f3n, also known as the kidney, is a vital organ that plays several important roles in the body. It serves as a donor of glutamine during periods of stress, thereby enhancing the availability of this amino acid. Additionally, the kidney is implicated in various metabolic disorders, and in certain cases of glucogenosis, renal transplantation may be necessary. Furthermore, the kidney is involved in glucose metabolism and can be affected by insulin resistance, which contributes to the development of metabolic syndrome. Overall, Ri\u00f1\u00f3n is essential for maintaining metabolic balance and responding to physiological challenges."}{"title": "C\u00c1LCIO:Calcium is a chemical element that plays a crucial role in various cellular processes, including muscle contraction and neurotransmitter release."}{"title": "C\u00c9LULAS \u0392:C\u00c9LULAS \u0392, or beta cells, are insulin-producing cells located in the pancreas that play a crucial role in glucose metabolism. These cells are responsible for the secretion of insulin, a hormone that regulates blood sugar levels. The secretion of insulin from beta cells is influenced by various factors, including the presence of GLP-1 (glucagon-like peptide-1), which enhances their function."}{"title": "NADH:NADH is a coenzyme that plays a key role in the production of ATP during cellular respiration."}{"title": "FADH:FADH is another coenzyme involved in the electron transport chain, contributing to ATP production."}{"title": "CADENCIAS DE INSULINA:Insulin pulses refer to the rhythmic release of insulin from beta cells in response to glucose levels."}{"title": "PROINSULINA:Proinsulin is a precursor to insulin, which is converted into insulin and C-peptide in the pancreas."}{"title": "KREBS CYCLE:The Krebs cycle, also known as the citric acid cycle or tricarboxylic acid (TCA) cycle, is a series of chemical reactions utilized by all aerobic organisms to generate energy. This cycle involves the oxidation of acetate, which is derived from carbohydrates, fats, and proteins, ultimately contributing to the production of adenosine triphosphate (ATP), the energy currency of the cell."}{"title": "ACCORD:The ACCORD study was a clinical trial that investigated the effects of intensive glucose lowering in type 2 diabetes and its impact on mortality and cardiovascular events."}{"title": "GLUT4:GLUT4 is a glucose transporter protein that plays a crucial role in insulin-regulated glucose uptake in muscle and fat tissues, significantly affecting glucose metabolism."}{"title": "DIABETES TYPE 2:Diabetes Type 2 is a chronic condition that significantly impacts the body's ability to process blood sugar (glucose). It is often linked to various cardiovascular risks and is commonly associated with high sugar consumption. Management of Diabetes Type 2 typically involves lifestyle changes, such as diet and exercise, as well as medication to help control blood sugar levels."}{"title": "HYPOGLYCEMIA:Hypoglycemia is a condition characterized by abnormally low blood sugar levels, which poses significant health concerns for various patient populations. It is particularly prevalent in individuals with glycogen storage diseases (GSD), especially in hepatic glucogenosis type I, where managing hypoglycemia is a primary treatment goal. Patients with GSDI often experience hypoglycemia, and it can also occur in GSDVI patients, particularly after fasting.\n\nBeyond glycogen storage diseases, hypoglycemia can arise from multiple factors, including tumors that produce insulin-like growth factor 2 (IGF-2). It is commonly observed in individuals with diabetes, especially those undergoing insulin therapy or taking other glucose-lowering medications. In diabetic patients, hypoglycemia may occur during dietary changes or as a result of medication administration.\n\nAdditionally, hypoglycemia can affect patients post-bariatric surgery, often linked to dumping syndrome, which leads to symptoms such as sweating and weakness. It can also manifest in individuals with acute adrenal insufficiency, contributing to low blood sugar levels. Overall, hypoglycemia is a multifaceted condition that requires careful management across various medical contexts."}{"title": "FETOPLACENTAL UNIT:The fetoplacental unit refers to the combined functions of the fetus and placenta, which influence maternal metabolism and insulin sensitivity during pregnancy."}{"title": "LEPTIN:Leptin is a hormone produced by adipose (fat) tissue that plays a crucial role in regulating energy balance and metabolism. It influences insulin sensitivity and appetite, particularly during pregnancy. Research has shown that leptin levels are significantly altered in patients with anorexia nervosa, where low levels of the hormone correlate with reduced body weight. This indicates that leptin is not only important for general energy regulation but also has specific implications for individuals with eating disorders, such as anorexia nervosa."}{"title": "SPANISH SOCIETY OF ENDOCRINOLOGY AND NUTRITION:The Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition (SEEN) is a professional organization dedicated to the study and management of endocrine and nutritional issues. This includes a focus on endocrine disorders such as diabetes mellitus and metabolic control. SEEN plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and conducting research related to endocrine and nutritional health, particularly in the area of diabetes management. Through its efforts, the organization aims to enhance understanding and improve the management of these critical health issues."}{"title": "MEZQUITA-RAYA P:Mezquita-Raya P is an author affiliated with the Diabetes Mellitus Working Group of the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition. They have made significant contributions to the development of guidelines focused on the management of hypoglycemia, particularly in the context of diabetes patients. Mezquita-Raya P is also recognized for their involvement in the creation of a document that addresses the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "REYES-GARC\u00cdA R:Reyes-Garc\u00eda R is an author associated with the document on the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in diabetes patients."}{"title": "MORENO-P\u00c9REZ O:Moreno-P\u00e9rez O is an author associated with the document on the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in diabetes patients."}{"title": "MU\u00d1OZ-TORRES M:Mu\u00f1oz-Torres M is an author associated with the document on the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in diabetes patients."}{"title": "MERINO-TORRES JF:Merino-Torres JF is an author associated with the document on the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in diabetes patients."}{"title": "GORGOJO-MART\u00cdNEZ JJ:Gorgojo-Mart\u00ednez JJ is an author associated with the document on the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in diabetes patients."}{"title": "NORADRENALINE:Noradrenaline is a hormone that plays a role in the body's response to low blood sugar levels, stimulating glucose production."}{"title": "PANCREATIC TUMORS:Pancreatic tumors can lead to hyperinsulinism, causing episodes of hypoglycemia in affected individuals."}{"title": "AUTOIMMUNE DISEASES:Autoimmune diseases can lead to the production of antibodies against insulin, contributing to hypoglycemia."}{"title": "CETOACIDOSIS DIAB\u00c9TICA:Cetoacidosis diab\u00e9tica, also known as diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), is a severe metabolic complication of diabetes mellitus. It is characterized by hyperglycemia, hyperketonemia, and metabolic acidosis, which can lead to a dangerous buildup of acids in the bloodstream. This condition often requires urgent medical intervention due to its serious nature. The body produces high levels of ketones during this process, which can also increase the production of uric acid due to metabolic changes. Symptoms of diabetic ketoacidosis include high blood sugar levels, the presence of ketones in the urine, and acidosis, making it a critical condition that necessitates immediate treatment."}{"title": "SEANQUISIT ER:Seanquist ER is an author involved in the workgroup of the American Diabetes Association and the Endocrine Society, focusing on hypoglycemia and diabetes management."}{"title": "CAD:CAD, or Coronary Artery Disease, is a condition that can complicate diabetes management and requires specific dietary considerations. However, the term CAD is also used to refer to diabetic ketoacidosis, a serious complication of diabetes characterized by high levels of ketones in the blood due to insufficient insulin. This condition leads to metabolic acidosis and is a critical health concern for individuals with diabetes. It is important to differentiate between these two meanings of CAD, as one pertains to heart health and the other to a severe metabolic state resulting from diabetes."}{"title": "UMPIERREZ G:G. Umpierrez is a researcher who has contributed to the literature on diabetic emergencies, including diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "WOLFSDORF J:J. Wolfsdorf is a researcher and author of consensus statements regarding diabetic ketoacidosis in infants, children, and adolescents."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS METAB\u00d3LICA:ACIDOSIS METAB\u00d3LICA, or metabolic acidosis, is a medical condition characterized by an excess of acid in the body fluids. This condition can arise from various underlying issues, including kidney dysfunction, where the kidneys fail to adequately remove acid from the body. It is often associated with diabetic ketoacidosis, a severe complication of diabetes, and can also occur in patients with conditions such as VIPoma, which leads to severe diarrhea and electrolyte imbalances.\n\nIn addition to these causes, metabolic acidosis can lead to the redistribution of phosphate, which is particularly relevant in the context of hypophosphatemia. It is also recognized as a complication in patients with renal insufficiency, where it can adversely affect their nutritional status. Furthermore, metabolic acidosis may manifest in infants suffering from glucose-galactose malabsorption, typically resulting from severe dehydration and diarrhea.\n\nOverall, metabolic acidosis is a complex condition that can arise from multiple factors, including metabolic disturbances and renal impairment, and it requires careful management to address the underlying causes and prevent further complications."}{"title": "CETOACIDOSIS:Cetoacidosis is a serious metabolic condition primarily associated with diabetes, particularly diabetic ketoacidosis, which occurs when the body produces high levels of ketones due to insufficient insulin. This condition can lead to elevated blood sugar levels and is a significant complication for individuals with diabetes. Additionally, ketoacidosis can also occur in adults with Maple Syrup Urine Disease, often triggered by intercurrent illnesses. Overall, cetoacidosis is characterized by the body's excessive production of ketones, making it a critical health concern that requires prompt medical attention."}{"title": "SHH:SHH, or Hyperglycemic Hyperosmolar State, is a severe complication of diabetes that results in high blood sugar levels without significant ketoacidosis."}{"title": "CATECHOLAMINES:Catecholamines are hormones produced by the adrenal glands, which include epinephrine and norepinephrine. These hormones play a crucial role in increasing blood glucose levels and counteracting insulin. Additionally, the excess production of catecholamines is a significant indicator in diagnosing pheochromocytomas, a type of tumor that can affect adrenal gland function."}{"title": "GROWTH HORMONE:Growth Hormone (GH) is a crucial hormone that plays a significant role in growth, cell reproduction, and regeneration, as well as influencing glucose metabolism. In patients with Anorexia Nervosa, GH levels are found to be elevated; however, this is accompanied by a decrease in Insulin-like Growth Factor 1 (IGF-1) due to resistance to GH. Additionally, GH levels may be diminished in individuals with liver disease, which can negatively impact metabolism and muscle mass. Furthermore, GH is being explored as a potential anti-aging treatment for older adults, although it is not an approved indication and carries various effects and risks. Overall, Growth Hormone is integral to several physiological processes, but its levels and effects can vary significantly depending on health conditions and age."}{"title": "GLYCOGENOLYSIS:Glycogenolysis is the biochemical process of breaking down glycogen into glucose, playing a crucial role in maintaining blood sugar levels, particularly during periods of fasting or intense physical activity. This process involves the degradation of glycogen and can be influenced by various conditions, including glucogenosis, which may alter the normal functioning of glycogenolysis."}{"title": "HORMONES:"}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIC HYPEROSMOLAR STATE:HYPERGLYCEMIC HYPEROSMOLAR STATE is a serious medical condition primarily affecting individuals with diabetes. It is characterized by extremely high blood sugar levels and increased osmolality, which can lead to neurological symptoms and, in severe cases, potential coma. The condition is often associated with significant dehydration, making it a critical health issue that requires prompt medical attention."}{"title": "DIABETIC KETOACIDOSIS:Diabetic ketoacidosis is a serious complication of diabetes that arises when the body produces high levels of ketones due to insufficient insulin. This condition leads to metabolic acidosis, characterized by a dangerous buildup of acids in the blood. Key indicators of diabetic ketoacidosis include high blood sugar levels, the presence of ketones in the urine, and acidosis. It is a critical medical emergency that requires prompt treatment to prevent severe health consequences."}{"title": "KITABCHI:A researcher who has contributed to the understanding of hyperglycemic crises in adult patients with diabetes."}{"title": "UMPIRERZ:A researcher involved in the study of hyperglycemic crises and diabetes management."}{"title": "MILES:A researcher who has co-authored studies on hyperglycemic crises in diabetes."}{"title": "FISHER:A researcher who has contributed to the literature on diabetes care and hyperglycemic crises."}{"title": "SALINE SOLUTION:Saline solution is a treatment method that involves the infusion of isotonic saline to correct fluid and electrolyte imbalances in patients experiencing hyperglycemic crises. This therapeutic approach is essential for restoring proper hydration and electrolyte levels in individuals facing such medical emergencies."}{"title": "LETARGO:A state of sluggishness or lack of energy, which can occur in patients with severe hyperglycemia."}{"title": "HEMIPARESIA:A condition characterized by weakness on one side of the body, which can be a neurological symptom of severe hyperglycemia."}{"title": "HEMIANOPSIA:A visual field defect that can occur in patients with neurological symptoms due to hyperglycemia."}{"title": "COMA:COMA refers to a state of deep unconsciousness that can arise from various severe medical conditions. Specifically, it can result from severe hyperglycemic conditions, where high blood sugar levels lead to a loss of consciousness. Additionally, coma can also occur due to severe hyponatremia, a condition characterized by dangerously low sodium levels in the blood. This serious medical state indicates a critical impairment of brain function, necessitating immediate medical attention."}{"title": "HYPEROSMOLALITY:A condition of increased osmolality in the blood, which is a key factor in hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "HYPERVENTILATION:A condition of rapid or deep breathing that can occur in response to metabolic disturbances, including those seen in diabetic crises."}{"title": "INFECTION:Infection refers to the invasion of the body by harmful pathogens, including pathogenic microorganisms, which can lead to disease and complicate recovery in various medical contexts. It is particularly relevant for patients undergoing nutritional support, especially in hematological settings, where the risk of infection is heightened. Additionally, infection can be a precipitating factor for hyperglycemic crises, necessitating prompt identification and treatment in affected individuals. In patients with pancreatitis, infection can arise as a complication, potentially leading to further health issues. Furthermore, the use of non-tunneled catheters for venous access is associated with an increased risk of infection. Overall, infection poses significant challenges in the management and recovery of patients, particularly those undergoing treatments such as bone marrow transplantation."}{"title": "SGLT2 INHIBITORS:A class of medications that can precipitate diabetic ketoacidosis and should be suspended in patients experiencing hyperglycemic crises.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "JOHN WILEY & SONS:John Wiley & Sons is a publishing company that published the work on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hypersmolar state in 2004."}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIC HYPERSMOLAR STATE:Hyperglycemic hypersmolar state is a severe condition associated with uncontrolled diabetes, leading to high blood sugar and dehydration."}{"title": "NEFROPAT\u00cdA DIAB\u00c9TICA:Diabetic nephropathy is a kidney-related complication associated with diabetes, which can ultimately lead to kidney failure. It is a significant area of research for Samuel Namara, highlighting its importance in understanding and addressing the health challenges posed by diabetes."}{"title": "NATIONAL KIDNEY FOUNDATION:The National Kidney Foundation is an organization dedicated to promoting kidney health and managing kidney diseases. It provides comprehensive guidelines and resources for various aspects of kidney health, including the evaluation, classification, and management of chronic kidney disease. Additionally, the foundation offers specific guidelines for diabetic nephropathy and addresses bone metabolism and disease in the context of chronic kidney disease. Through its efforts, the National Kidney Foundation aims to enhance understanding and treatment of kidney-related conditions, ensuring that both healthcare professionals and patients have access to essential information and support."}{"title": "GLUCOTOXICIDAD:Glucotoxicity refers to the toxic effects of high glucose levels on cells, particularly in the context of diabetes."}{"title": "ALBUMINURIA:Albuminuria is the presence of albumin in the urine, which serves as a significant marker for kidney damage, particularly in individuals with diabetic nephropathy. This condition indicates that the kidneys are not functioning properly, and it is especially relevant for diabetic patients, as it can signal the onset of kidney-related complications associated with diabetes."}{"title": "PROTEINURIA:Proteinuria is the presence of excess proteins in the urine, indicating kidney damage, particularly in diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "ATROFIA TUBULAR:Tubular atrophy is a condition where the kidney tubules shrink, often associated with chronic kidney disease, including diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "FIBROSIS INTERSTICIAL:Interstitial fibrosis is the accumulation of fibrous tissue in the kidney, which can occur in diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "HYPERTENSI\u00d3N ARTERIAL:Hypertension Arterial, commonly referred to as hypertension, is a chronic condition characterized by elevated blood pressure. This condition plays a significant role in the overall health profile of affected individuals. It is particularly noteworthy as a common comorbidity in patients with diabetes, where it can exacerbate health complications. Additionally, hypertension is recognized as a significant risk factor for the development and progression of diabetic nephropathy, highlighting its critical impact on kidney health in diabetic patients."}{"title": "HIPERFILTRACI\u00d3N:Hyperfiltration is an increase in the glomerular filtration rate, often seen in the early stages of diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "MICROHEMATURIA:Microhematuria is the presence of small amounts of blood in the urine, which can indicate kidney issues unrelated to diabetes."}{"title": "PODOCITOS:Podocytes are specialized cells in the kidney that play a crucial role in filtering blood; their damage is an early sign of diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "MATRIZ MESANGIAL:Mesangial matrix refers to the connective tissue in the kidney glomeruli, which can expand in diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD RENAL CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic kidney disease (enfermedad renal cr\u00f3nica, ERC) is a long-term medical condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to function effectively, often associated with diabetes. It is defined by a glomerular filtration rate (GFR) below 60 ml/min for at least three months, which can lead to various health complications. The disease is classified into different stages, with stage 3 considered to be of high cardiovascular risk, and stages 4-5 or those requiring dialysis classified as very high risk.\n\nManagement of chronic kidney disease necessitates dietary restrictions and specialized nutritional formulas, particularly in advanced stages. It requires careful monitoring of phosphorus intake to prevent further complications. Additionally, chronic kidney disease can invalidate the results of catecholamine and metanephrine tests used in diagnosing pheochromocytoma. The condition also complicates the management of acute diarrhea, necessitating special attention in treatment. Overall, chronic kidney disease is a serious condition that demands comprehensive medical and nutritional care."}{"title": "DIABETIC NEPHROPATHY:Diabetic nephropathy is a kidney disease that results from diabetes, characterized by the presence of albuminuria and reduced glomerular filtration rate."}{"title": "RETINOPATHY:Retinopathy is a diabetes-related eye condition that can lead to vision loss, often requiring treatment to prevent progression."}{"title": "VEGF:Vascular Endothelial Growth Factor (VEGF) is a signal protein that plays a crucial role in the formation of blood vessels. It is particularly significant in the context of various medical conditions, including diabetic retinopathy, where it has been linked to the disease's pathogenesis. VEGF promotes the growth of blood vessels, making it a key target in treatments for diabetic retinopathy. Additionally, it is mentioned in relation to POEMS syndrome, highlighting its broader implications in vascular biology and disease. Overall, VEGF is an important protein in both the development of certain diseases and the therapeutic strategies employed to manage them."}{"title": "PANRETINAL LASER COAGULATION:Panretinal laser coagulation is a treatment method used to reduce the risk of vision loss in patients with proliferative diabetic retinopathy."}{"title": "DIABETES-2019:Diabetes-2019 refers to a publication or event related to diabetes care and research, specifically focusing on diabetic retinopathy and its classifications."}{"title": "WILKINSON C:Wilkinson C is an author who contributed to the proposed international clinical diabetic retinopathy and diabetic macular edema disease severity scales."}{"title": "KLEIN R:Klein R is an author who contributed to the proposed international clinical diabetic retinopathy and diabetic macular edema disease severity scales."}{"title": "GARDNER TW:Gardner TW is an author who contributed to the proposed international clinical diabetic retinopathy and diabetic macular edema disease severity scales."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 1:Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 (DM1) is a chronic autoimmune disease characterized by the destruction of insulin-producing beta cells in the pancreas, leading to little or no insulin production. This condition typically develops in children and young adults, although it can be diagnosed at any age, as evidenced by cases where individuals are diagnosed in their late twenties. The lack of insulin results in high blood sugar levels, necessitating careful management of diet, physical activity, and insulin levels to maintain blood glucose control. Additionally, individuals with Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 may be predisposed to other autoimmune conditions, such as Klinefelter syndrome. Overall, effective management of DM1 is crucial to prevent various complications associated with the disease."}{"title": "EDEMA MACULAR:Edema macular is a condition that occurs when fluid accumulates in the macula, leading to vision impairment, often associated with diabetic retinopathy."}{"title": "RETINOPAT\u00cdA DIAB\u00c9TICA:"}{"title": "DIABETIC RETINOPATHY:Diabetic retinopathy is a complication of diabetes that significantly impacts the eyes. It is characterized by damage to the retina, which occurs as a result of prolonged high blood sugar levels. This condition can lead to vision impairment and, if left untreated, may result in blindness. Additionally, diabetic retinopathy can worsen with rapid improvements in glycemic control, highlighting the importance of careful management of blood sugar levels in individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "EDEMA MACULAR DIAB\u00c9TICO:Diabetic macular edema (DME) is a condition characterized by retinal thickening and swelling affecting the macula, which can lead to decreased visual acuity and blindness."}{"title": "ANTONETTI DA:Antonetti DA is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of diabetic retinopathy and its complications."}{"title": "DIABETES CONTROL AND COMPLICATIONS TRIAL RESEARCH GROUP:The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial Research Group is a collaborative entity that conducted the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT). This research group focused on studying the effects of strict glycemic control on various complications associated with diabetes, particularly diabetic retinopathy. Their work aimed to understand how effective diabetes management can influence the development and progression of complications, thereby contributing valuable insights to the field of diabetes care."}{"title": "EMBARAZO:EMBARAZO, or pregnancy, is a physiological condition that significantly influences various health aspects, including the progression of retinopathy diab\u00e9tica in some patients. It is characterized by specific dietary recommendations tailored to different age groups, particularly focusing on pregnant individuals aged 14-18 years. These recommendations include defined nutrient intake levels that vary according to the age of the pregnant individual, with metrics established for those under 18 years, 19-30 years, and 31-50 years.\n\nDuring pregnancy, there is a notable impact on nutritional needs and energy requirements, which fluctuate throughout the different trimesters. Additionally, pregnancy affects thyroid function and hormone levels, necessitating careful management of any thyroid-related issues. Overall, EMBARAZO encompasses a range of health and demographic considerations, highlighting the importance of tailored dietary and health management strategies for pregnant individuals."}{"title": "DIABETIC MACULAR EDEMA:Diabetic macular edema is a condition that involves the swelling of the retina and affects the macula, often resulting from diabetic retinopathy."}{"title": "TOMOGRAF\u00cdA DE COHERENCIA \u00d3PTICA:Tomograf\u00eda de coherencia \u00f3ptica (OCT) is a non-invasive imaging technology used to capture high-resolution images of the retina, often used in diagnosing diabetic eye diseases."}{"title": "ISQUEMIA MICROVASCULAR:Isquemia microvascular refers to a condition where small blood vessels are obstructed, often leading to complications in patients with diabetes."}{"title": "ANEURISMA DE LA ARTERIA COMUNICANTE POSTERIOR:Aneurisma de la arteria comunicante posterior is a type of aneurysm that can occur in the brain, potentially affecting vision and other neurological functions."}{"title": "HEMORRAGIA V\u00cdTREO:Hemorragia v\u00edtreo is a condition characterized by bleeding into the vitreous humor of the eye, often associated with diabetic retinopathy."}{"title": "NEOPLASIA:Neoplasia refers to the abnormal growth of tissue, which can manifest as either benign or malignant forms. This condition can occur in various parts of the body, including the eyes and the larynx, as evidenced by findings from a CT scan of a patient. In this particular case, neoplasia is associated with the presence of a tumor that impacts the patient's medical condition, specifically affecting their nutritional needs."}{"title": "DIPLOPIA:Diplopia, or double vision, is a visual disturbance that can occur due to various conditions, including diabetic complications affecting the eye muscles."}{"title": "PTOSIS:Ptosis is a condition characterized by the drooping of one or both eyelids, which can be associated with neurological issues in diabetic patients."}{"title": "DIABETIC NEUROPATHY:Diabetic neuropathy is a heterogeneous group of disorders that result from nerve damage due to diabetes, leading to various clinical manifestations."}{"title": "POLYNEUROPATHY:Polyneuropathy is a condition that affects multiple peripheral nerves, often seen in diabetic patients as a complication of diabetes."}{"title": "GLUCOSE CONTROL:Glucose control refers to the management of blood sugar levels in individuals with diabetes to prevent complications such as neuropathy."}{"title": "FOOT CARE:Foot care is an essential aspect of diabetes management to prevent complications such as foot injuries and infections, particularly in patients with neuropathy."}{"title": "HEART DISEASE:Heart disease encompasses various cardiovascular conditions that are more prevalent in individuals with diabetes, leading to increased mortality risk."}{"title": "NEUROPATHY:"}{"title": "ACUTE MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION:Acute myocardial infarction (AMI) is a medical emergency where blood flow to the heart is blocked, leading to heart damage, particularly prevalent among diabetic patients."}{"title": "AMERICAN COLLEGE OF CARDIOLOGY:The American College of Cardiology (ACC) is a prominent professional organization based in the USA dedicated to enhancing cardiovascular health through a multifaceted approach that includes education, research, and advocacy. The ACC plays a crucial role in providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management of cardiovascular health and diseases, particularly focusing on the care of patients with acute coronary syndromes. Additionally, the organization addresses broader health concerns by publishing guidelines for the management of overweight and obesity in adults, thereby contributing to disease prevention efforts. Through its initiatives, the ACC aims to improve patient outcomes and promote best practices in cardiovascular care."}{"title": "DCCT:The Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) is a landmark and pivotal study that demonstrated the significant benefits of intensive diabetes management in reducing microvascular complications among patients with Type 1 Diabetes. This groundbreaking research established the importance of rigorous control of blood glucose levels to improve health outcomes for individuals living with this condition."}{"title": "EDIC:The EDIC, or Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications, is a long-term follow-up study of patients with Type 1 Diabetes who were initially included in the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT). This study tracks the health outcomes of these patients over a period of 27 years, assessing the long-term effects of diabetes management interventions. The EDIC study aims to provide valuable insights into the complications and management of Type 1 Diabetes, building on the foundational data gathered during the DCCT."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME CORONARIO AGUDO:Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS) refers to a group of conditions characterized by a sudden decrease in blood flow to the heart, which can lead to serious cardiovascular events. This syndrome is often associated with underlying health issues such as diabetes. Research suggests that the risk of developing acute coronary syndrome may be mitigated by dietary changes, specifically by increasing the weekly intake of fish."}{"title": "BETABLOQUEANTES:Beta-blockers, known as \"BETABLOQUEANTES,\" are a class of medications primarily used to manage various heart conditions, including acute coronary syndrome. They are particularly recommended for diabetic patients due to their beneficial effects on cardiovascular health. In critical care settings, these drugs are considered essential for managing patients' conditions effectively. Additionally, specific beta-blockers, such as propranolol and metoprolol, are utilized in burn patients to reduce muscle catabolism and enhance immune response, highlighting their versatility in treating different medical scenarios."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA CARD\u00cdACA:Insuficiencia card\u00edaca, or heart failure, is a medical condition characterized by the heart's inability to pump blood sufficiently to meet the body's needs. This chronic condition can lead to various complications, including fluid accumulation in the abdomen, which may be associated with ascitis quilosa. The incidence of heart failure has been found to be inversely related to fish consumption, suggesting dietary factors may play a role in its management. \n\nIn pediatric patients, heart failure significantly affects energy expenditure and may necessitate nutritional management, including adjustments in fluid and nutrient intake. Additionally, it is noted that heart failure is a precautionary consideration when using certain medications, such as lorcaserin. Furthermore, this condition can lead to hypervolemic hyponatremia, highlighting the importance of careful monitoring and management in affected individuals. Overall, insuficiencia card\u00edaca is a complex condition that requires comprehensive care and dietary considerations, particularly in vulnerable populations like children."}{"title": "DM1:DM1 refers to Type 1 Diabetes, a chronic condition characterized by the pancreas producing little or no insulin. It is a high-risk condition that is often associated with celiac disease. Additionally, individuals with Type 1 Diabetes may also manage other health issues, such as eating disorders, which can complicate the management of their diabetes."}{"title": "GUBITOSI-KLUG RA:Gubitosi-Klug RA is a researcher associated with the DCCT/EDIC Research Group, contributing to studies on diabetes management and outcomes."}{"title": "LACHIN JM:Lachin JM is a researcher involved in the DCCT/EDIC Research Group, focusing on long-term diabetes outcomes."}{"title": "NATHAN DM:Nathan DM is a prominent researcher in diabetes care, part of the DCCT/EDIC Research Group."}{"title": "AACE:The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists (AACE) is a professional organization dedicated to providing comprehensive medical guidelines for various endocrine disorders. Among its contributions, AACE offers specific guidelines for the management of thyroid nodules, including recommendations for the performance of fine-needle aspiration biopsy (PAAF). Additionally, the organization is recognized for its extensive guidelines on the treatment and management of diabetes, further emphasizing its role in advancing clinical practices in endocrinology."}{"title": "CARDIOVASCULAR OUTCOMES:Cardiovascular outcomes refer to the health events related to the heart and blood vessels, which are significant in the context of diabetes management."}{"title": "RETINOPATHY DIAB\u00c9TICA:Diabetic retinopathy is a diabetes complication that affects the eyes, leading to vision impairment and blindness if untreated."}{"title": "MICRO/MACROALBUMINURIA:Microalbuminuria and macroalbuminuria are conditions indicating the presence of albumin in urine, which can be a sign of kidney damage in diabetes patients."}{"title": "CARVEDILOL:Carvedilol is a non-selective beta-blocker with antioxidant effects, used to improve insulin sensitivity in patients."}{"title": "GLIFLOZINAS:Gliflozinas are a class of medications (SGLT2 inhibitors) used in the management of type 2 diabetes, affecting glucagon levels."}{"title": "BAGNARDI V:Bagnardi V is a co-author of a meta-analysis that studies the relationship between alcohol consumption and disease incidence."}{"title": "ZAMBON A:Zambon A is a researcher involved in a meta-analysis examining alcohol consumption and its health impacts."}{"title": "LA VECCHIA C:La Vecchia C is a co-author of a meta-analysis on alcohol consumption and disease risk."}{"title": "COSTANZO S:Costanzo S is a researcher who studied cardiovascular and overall mortality risk in relation to alcohol consumption."}{"title": "DI CASTELNUOVO A:Di Castelnuovo A is a co-author of a study on the relationship between alcohol consumption and cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "DONATI MB:Donati MB is a researcher who contributed to the study of alcohol consumption and its effects on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "IACOVIELLO L:Iacoviello L is a co-author of research on alcohol consumption and cardiovascular disease risk."}{"title": "DE GAETANO G:De Gaetano G is a researcher involved in studies related to alcohol consumption and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "GARBER AJ:Garber AJ is a researcher actively engaged in the development of obesity management guidelines. He serves as a reviewer for the AACE/ACE guidelines pertaining to obesity management, contributing his expertise to ensure the guidelines are comprehensive and effective. Additionally, Garber AJ is an author of a consensus statement that addresses diabetes management, with a particular emphasis on the associated risks of cardiovascular disease. Through these roles, he plays a significant part in shaping clinical practices related to obesity and diabetes."}{"title": "ABDELHAMID AS:Abdelhamid AS is a researcher who studied omega-3 fatty acids for the prevention of cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "BROWN TJ:Brown TJ is a co-author of a study on omega-3 fatty acids and cardiovascular disease prevention."}{"title": "BRAINARD JS:Brainard JS is a researcher involved in the study of omega-3 fatty acids for cardiovascular health."}{"title": "BISWAS P:Biswas P is a co-author of research on omega-3 fatty acids and their effects on cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "THORPE GC:Thorpe GC is a researcher who contributed to the study of omega-3 fatty acids in cardiovascular disease prevention."}{"title": "MOORE HJ:Moore HJ is a co-author of a study on omega-3 fatty acids and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "FERRANNINI E:Ferrannini E is a prominent researcher known for studying the metabolic response to SGLT2 inhibition in patients with type 2 diabetes. In addition to his research contributions, Ferrannini E has also played a significant role as an author, contributing to the management guidelines for diabetes care. His work has been influential in advancing the understanding and treatment of diabetes."}{"title": "MUSCELLI E:Muscelli E is a co-author of research on the effects of SGLT2 inhibitors in type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "FRASCERRA S:Frascerra S is a researcher involved in the study of SGLT2 inhibitors and their metabolic effects."}{"title": "FOGARI R:Fogari R is a researcher known for studying the relationship between urinary albumin excretion and blood pressure in diabetic patients."}{"title": "ZOPPI A:Zoppi A is a co-author of significant research focusing on the relationship between urinary albumin excretion and nocturnal blood pressure in hypertensive patients with type II diabetes mellitus. Additionally, Zoppi A has contributed to studies concerning blood pressure and diabetes management, highlighting their involvement in important medical research aimed at understanding and improving health outcomes for individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "MALAMANI GD:Malamani GD is a co-author of a study that investigates the relationship between urinary albumin excretion and nocturnal blood pressure in hypertensive patients with type II diabetes mellitus. In addition to this role, Malamani GD is also recognized as a researcher focused on the study of hypertension in diabetic patients, contributing valuable insights to this important area of medical research."}{"title": "LAZZARI P:Lazzari P is a co-author of research focusing on the relationship between blood pressure and diabetes. Specifically, Lazzari P contributed to a study examining urinary albumin excretion and nocturnal blood pressure in hypertensive patients with type II diabetes mellitus. This work highlights Lazzari P's involvement in important research addressing the health challenges faced by individuals with diabetes and hypertension."}{"title": "ALBONICO B:Albonico B is a researcher who has contributed to the field of diabetes management, particularly focusing on the relationship between blood pressure and diabetes. They co-authored a study that specifically examined urinary albumin excretion and nocturnal blood pressure in hypertensive patients with type II diabetes mellitus. Through their work, Albonico B has provided valuable insights into the interplay between hypertension and diabetes, highlighting the importance of monitoring these conditions in affected patients."}{"title": "CORRADI L:Corradi L is a co-author of a study that investigates the relationship between urinary albumin excretion and nocturnal blood pressure in hypertensive patients with type II diabetes mellitus. Additionally, Corradi L has contributed to research focused on hypertension in patients with type 2 diabetes, highlighting their involvement in important studies related to these health conditions."}{"title": "METFORMIN:Metformin is a medication commonly prescribed for managing type 2 diabetes. Mar\u00eda takes Metformin in a dosage of 850 mg three times a day. This medication works by reducing glucose production in the liver and improving insulin sensitivity, which helps to control blood sugar levels. Additionally, Metformin is often used in combination with liraglutide to enhance glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "PIOGLITAZONE:Pioglitazone is a medication that reduces insulin resistance and improves lipid profiles in patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "GLINIDAS:Glinidas are a class of medications that increase insulin secretion from the pancreas, with a short duration of action."}{"title": "TYPE II DIABETES MELLITUS:Type II diabetes mellitus is a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose), often requiring medication and lifestyle changes."}{"title": "REDON J:Redon J is a co-author of a study on ambulatory blood pressure and microalbuminuria in essential hypertension."}{"title": "LIAO Y:Liao Y is a co-author of a study on ambulatory blood pressure and microalbuminuria in essential hypertension."}{"title": "LOZANO JV:Lozano JV is a co-author of a study on ambulatory blood pressure and microalbuminuria in essential hypertension."}{"title": "MIRALLES A:Miralles A is a co-author of a study on ambulatory blood pressure and microalbuminuria in essential hypertension."}{"title": "PASCUAL JM:Pascual JM is a co-author of a study on ambulatory blood pressure and microalbuminuria in essential hypertension."}{"title": "COOPER RS:Cooper RS is a co-author of a study on ambulatory blood pressure and microalbuminuria in essential hypertension."}{"title": "SARAFIDIS PA:Sarafidis PA is a notable figure in the field of medical research, recognized for his contributions to the understanding of metabolic conditions. He is a co-author of a study that explores the metabolic effects of beta blockers in the treatment of hypertension, highlighting the implications of these medications on metabolic health. Additionally, Sarafidis PA has authored a review that examines the history of metabolic syndrome, providing insights into its evolution and significance in contemporary medicine. Through these works, he has contributed to the broader discourse on the intersection of cardiovascular health and metabolic disorders."}{"title": "BAKRIS GL:Bakris GL is a co-author of a study discussing the metabolic effects of beta blockers in hypertension treatment."}{"title": "SITAGLIPTINA:Sitagliptina is an oral antidiabetic medication primarily used in the treatment of type 2 diabetes. It functions by increasing insulin release and decreasing glucose production in the liver, thereby helping to control blood sugar levels. In addition to its general use for type 2 diabetes, Sitagliptina has also been utilized in the treatment regimen for patients with MNGIE (Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy), indicating its versatility in managing blood sugar levels in different patient populations."}{"title": "VILDAGLIPTINA:Vildagliptina is a diabetes medication that requires dose adjustment based on renal function."}{"title": "SAXAGLIPTINA:Saxagliptina is a medication for type 2 diabetes that is eliminated primarily through the kidneys and requires dose adjustment in renal impairment."}{"title": "DPP-4:Dipeptidyl peptidase 4 (DPP-4) is an enzyme that inactivates incretin hormones, which are important for insulin regulation."}{"title": "GLP-1:GLP-1, or Glucagon-like peptide-1, is an incretin hormone that plays a crucial role in the regulation of insulin secretion and blood sugar levels. It is a gastrointestinal hormone produced by intestinal L cells in the distal intestine, released after eating. GLP-1 enhances insulin secretion, lowers blood sugar levels, and is involved in various physiological processes, including gastric emptying and appetite regulation. \n\nThis peptide hormone exerts anorexigenic effects, meaning it helps reduce appetite, and it inhibits signals from neuropeptide Y, which is associated with hunger. GLP-1's functions are influenced by dietary factors such as fiber intake and short-chain fatty acids. It is particularly relevant in the context of obesity treatment, as it regulates glucose metabolism and energy expenditure. Additionally, GLP-1 is the target of medications like liraglutide, which are designed to leverage its effects for therapeutic purposes. Overall, GLP-1 is integral to maintaining glucose homeostasis and managing appetite."}{"title": "GIP:GIP, or Gastric Inhibitory Polypeptide, is an incretin hormone that plays a significant role in the regulation of insulin."}{"title": "ERC:ERC, or Enfermedad Renal Cr\u00f3nica, refers to chronic kidney disease (CKD), a condition that significantly impacts the management of diabetes medications. Individuals with ERC require careful dietary management, particularly concerning their intake of phosphorus and protein, to maintain their health and mitigate the progression of the disease."}{"title": "AHREN B.:Ahren B. is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of GLP-1 and its effects."}{"title": "DRUCKER DJ:Drucker DJ is a researcher known for his work on glucagon-like peptides and their therapeutic potential."}{"title": "HORM METAB RES:Horm Metab Res is a scientific journal that publishes research related to hormones and metabolism."}{"title": "REV ENDOC METAB DISORD:Rev Endocr Metab Disord is a journal that focuses on the endocrine and metabolic disorders."}{"title": "SUSTAIN-6:SUSTAIN-6 is a clinical trial that studied the effects of semaglutide on renal outcomes."}{"title": "LEADER:LEADER is a clinical trial that investigated the effects of liraglutide on albuminuria."}{"title": "T\u00daBULO PROXIMAL:The proximal tubule is a part of the nephron in the kidney where GLP-1 influences natriuresis and glucose handling."}{"title": "C\u00c9LULAS DE LA CAPA MUSCULAR VASCULAR:Muscle layer cells in blood vessels where GLP-1 receptors are present, suggesting a role in vasodilation."}{"title": "SISTEMA RENINA-ANGIOTENSINA-ALDOSTERONA:The \"SISTEMA RENINA-ANGIOTENSINA-ALDOSTERONA\" is a crucial hormonal system that plays a significant role in regulating blood pressure and maintaining fluid balance in the body. This system is activated during pregnancy, highlighting its importance in physiological changes that occur during this period. Additionally, it can be affected in patients with eating disorders, indicating its relevance in various health conditions. Furthermore, the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system may interact with the effects of GLP-1, suggesting a complex interplay between different hormonal systems in the regulation of blood pressure. Overall, the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system is essential for cardiovascular health and fluid homeostasis."}{"title": "DM2:DM2 refers to Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, a chronic condition that affects the way the body processes blood sugar (glucose). It is a metabolic disorder characterized by insulin resistance, which leads to elevated blood sugar levels. Additionally, DM2 is associated with various lipid abnormalities, further complicating the metabolic profile of individuals affected by this condition."}{"title": "INSULINA BASAL:Insulina basal refers to a type of insulin used to control blood sugar levels in patients with diabetes. It is typically administered once or twice daily to help maintain stable glucose levels throughout the day and night."}{"title": "INSULINA R\u00c1PIDA:Insulina r\u00e1pida is a type of fast-acting insulin utilized in the management of blood sugar levels for diabetic patients. It is specifically designed to address blood sugar spikes that occur during meals, making it an essential component of diabetes treatment. This insulin is administered subcutaneously to patients every six hours to effectively control their glycemia."}{"title": "INSULINA GLARGINA:Insulina Glargina is a long-acting insulin utilized by patients for the management of diabetes. It is administered at night to help control blood sugar levels effectively. This insulin formulation is particularly beneficial for maintaining steady insulin levels in the body, which is crucial for managing blood glucose levels in diabetic patients. Insulina Glargina is also noted for its role in diabetes management post-surgery and is used in the context of nutritional therapy, including in patients with Alzheimer's disease. It is specifically indicated for patients with type 2 diabetes, highlighting its importance in comprehensive diabetes care. Overall, Insulina Glargina serves as a vital medication for individuals seeking to regulate their blood sugar levels and improve their overall diabetes management."}{"title": "INSULINA REGULAR:Insulina regular is a transparent solution of zinc insulin crystals, primarily utilized in the treatment of diabetes. It is classified as a short-acting insulin, which is typically administered before meals to effectively manage blood sugar levels. This type of insulin is particularly important for individuals with diabetes, as it helps control blood sugar levels not only during meals but also before exercise. Additionally, insulina regular is used in the context of parenteral nutrition, highlighting its versatility in various treatment scenarios for patients requiring insulin therapy."}{"title": "INSULINA DETEMIR:Insulina detemir is a long-acting insulin that helps maintain blood sugar levels throughout the day and night."}{"title": "INSULINA GLULISINA:Insulina glulisina is a rapid-acting insulin analog that is utilized to control blood sugar levels, particularly during meals. It promotes the formation of monomers following subcutaneous administration, which enhances its effectiveness in managing diabetes. This type of insulin is specifically administered to patients to help regulate their blood glucose levels."}{"title": "SACIEDAD:Saciedad refers to the feeling of fullness or satisfaction after eating, which is influenced by hormones like GLP-1."}{"title": "INSULINA BIF\u00c1SICA:Insulina bif\u00e1sica refers to a mixed insulin formulation that combines both short-acting and long-acting insulin to manage blood sugar levels."}{"title": "COMORBILIDADES:Comorbilidades refer to the presence of one or more additional conditions that occur alongside a primary condition, which can complicate the management and prognosis of the primary illness. For instance, in patients with diabetes, cardiovascular disease may be a common comorbidity. Similarly, in individuals with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), the existence of additional comorbidities can further complicate treatment and affect overall health outcomes."}{"title": "GLP-1 AGONISTS:"}{"title": "INSULINA LISPRO:Insulina lispro is a rapid-acting insulin that is utilized by patients as needed for the management of blood sugar levels. It is designed to mimic the quick insulin secretion response observed in non-diabetic individuals. This insulin is particularly effective in controlling blood sugar levels around meal times and during exercise, making it an essential component for individuals managing diabetes. Insulina lispro helps to ensure that blood sugar levels remain stable during periods of increased glucose intake, such as meals."}{"title": "INSULINA ASPART:Insulina aspart es un an\u00e1logo de insulina de acci\u00f3n r\u00e1pida que presenta una menor tendencia a la agregaci\u00f3n de mol\u00e9culas de insulina en presencia de zinc."}{"title": "FASTER ASPART:Faster aspart es un an\u00e1logo de insulina ultrarr\u00e1pido que presenta un inicio de absorci\u00f3n de insulina m\u00e1s precoz y una mayor acci\u00f3n en las primeras 2 horas."}{"title": "LISPRO ULTRARR\u00c1PIDA:Lispro ultrarr\u00e1pida es un an\u00e1logo de insulina en desarrollo que busca mejorar el control de la glucemia posprandial."}{"title": "LISPRO BIOCHAPERONA:Lispro biochaperona es un an\u00e1logo de insulina en desarrollo que tiene como objetivo mejorar la eficacia del tratamiento de la diabetes."}{"title": "MANUAL SEEN DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA:"}{"title": "PHARMACOLOGIC APPROACHES TO GLYCEMIC TREATMENT:A set of standards for medical care in diabetes that outlines pharmacologic approaches to glycemic treatment."}{"title": "UK PROSPECTIVE DIABETES STUDY GROUP:A research group that conducted the UK Prospective Diabetes Study, which compared intensive blood-glucose control with conventional treatment in type 2 diabetes patients."}{"title": "INSULIN INFUSION:A method of delivering insulin continuously through a subcutaneous device, compared to multiple daily injections."}{"title": "TYPE 2 DIABETES:Type 2 diabetes is a chronic condition that significantly impacts the body's ability to process blood sugar (glucose). It is often associated with obesity and various lifestyle factors, including diet. This form of diabetes can arise when the body becomes resistant to insulin or when the pancreas fails to produce sufficient insulin. Research has indicated that dietary influences play a crucial role in managing this condition, with studies suggesting that higher dietary fiber intake may lower the risk of developing Type 2 diabetes. Management of the condition can sometimes be achieved through lifestyle changes and the use of oral medications."}{"title": "GLYCEMIC CONTROL:Glycemic control refers to the management of blood glucose levels in individuals with diabetes, which is essential for preventing complications associated with the condition. This management often involves dietary adjustments and the use of medication to maintain optimal blood sugar levels. By effectively controlling glycemic levels, diabetic patients can reduce the risk of serious health issues and improve their overall well-being."}{"title": "LIPOHYPERTROPHY:A condition that can occur in diabetes patients due to repeated insulin injections in the same area, leading to erratic insulin absorption."}{"title": "LIPOATROPHY:A condition characterized by the loss of fat tissue, which can also affect insulin absorption in diabetes patients."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ-HUELGAS R:G\u00f3mez-Huelgas R is a researcher involved in the consensus document on the treatment of type 2 diabetes in patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ-CASTELAO A:Mart\u00ednez-Castelao A is a researcher who contributed to the consensus document regarding diabetes treatment in patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "ARTOLA S:Artola S is a researcher who is part of the group that developed the consensus document on diabetes treatment."}{"title": "G\u00d3RRIZ JL:G\u00f3rriz JL is a researcher associated with the consensus document on diabetes treatment in patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "MEN\u00c9NDEZ E:Men\u00e9ndez E is a researcher involved in the consensus document on diabetes treatment for patients with chronic kidney disease."}{"title": "BRUTTOMESSO D:Bruttomesso D is a researcher who has published studies comparing insulin infusion methods in type 1 diabetes patients."}{"title": "CRAZZOLARA D:Crazzolara D is a researcher who has contributed to studies on insulin infusion in type 1 diabetes patients."}{"title": "MARAN A:Maran A is a researcher involved in studies comparing insulin delivery methods in diabetes management."}{"title": "COSTA S:Costa S is a researcher who has worked on studies related to insulin treatment in diabetes patients."}{"title": "DAL POS M:Dal Pos M is a researcher who has contributed to studies on insulin treatment in diabetes management."}{"title": "GIRELLI A:Girelli A is a researcher involved in studies comparing insulin delivery methods in diabetes management."}{"title": "RE PAGLINIDA:Repaglinide is an oral medication used to treat Type 2 diabetes by stimulating insulin secretion from the pancreas."}{"title": "E-LACTANCIA:E-lactancia is a resource providing information on the safety of medications during lactation, accessible online."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA:Mar\u00eda is a patient who has faced several health challenges. She has experienced altered basal glucose levels and is currently undergoing treatment for prediabetes, which later progressed to a diagnosis of gestational diabetes. Additionally, Mar\u00eda presented with a superficial ulcer on her left foot, which is infected; however, the infection does not involve deeper structures."}{"title": "SOBRECARGA ORAL DE GLUCOSA:SOBRECARGA ORAL DE GLUCOSA (SOG) is a test used to diagnose diabetes, including gestational diabetes, by measuring blood glucose levels after consuming glucose."}{"title": "TEXAS SCALE:The Texas scale is a classification system used to assess the severity of ulcers, particularly in diabetic patients."}{"title": "WAGNER SCALE:The Wagner scale is a classification system for ulcers that categorizes them based on depth and presence of infection or ischemia."}{"title": "NICE:The National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE) is an organization that provides comprehensive guidelines related to healthcare. It focuses on various aspects of medical care, including the management of specific health conditions and the improvement of patient outcomes. NICE offers directives on the care of malnourished patients, ensuring that their nutritional needs are addressed effectively. Additionally, it provides guidelines for the prevention and management of diabetic foot problems, highlighting its commitment to addressing critical health issues and enhancing the quality of care across different patient populations."}{"title": "KAMEL KS:Kamel KS is a researcher focused on the pathophysiology of low urine pH in patients with uric acid stones. In addition to this area of study, Kamel KS has also made significant contributions to the understanding of acid-base problems associated with diabetic ketoacidosis. Through his research, Kamel KS aims to enhance the knowledge surrounding these critical health issues."}{"title": "PALMER BF:PALMER BF is a medical professional and researcher recognized for his contributions to the understanding of electrolyte and acid-base disturbances in patients with diabetes mellitus. He co-authored a significant paper on this topic, highlighting his expertise and commitment to advancing knowledge in this area of medicine."}{"title": "WOLFSDORF JI:Wolfsdorf JI is a distinguished medical professional known for significant contributions to pediatric and adolescent diabetes management. He has played a vital role in the development of the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines, specifically addressing diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state. As a member of the International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes, Wolfsdorf has actively participated in shaping clinical practice consensus on diabetes management. In addition to his work in diabetes, he has authored research on cornstarch regimens for glycogen storage disease and has investigated the relationship between metabolic control and renal dysfunction in type 1 glycogen storage disease. Through his research and clinical guidelines, Wolfsdorf JI has made substantial contributions to the understanding and management of these complex medical conditions."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL SOCIETY FOR PEDIATRIC AND ADOLESCENT DIABETES:The International Society for Pediatric and Adolescent Diabetes is a global organization dedicated to enhancing the care and management of diabetes in children and adolescents. It provides comprehensive guidelines and support aimed at improving the health outcomes of young individuals affected by diabetes. The organization emphasizes the importance of research and education in its mission to advance the understanding and treatment of diabetes in this specific age group."}{"title": "FLUIDOTERAPIA:FLUIDOTERAPIA, or fluid therapy, is a vital medical treatment that involves the administration of fluids to patients to maintain hydration and electrolyte balance. It is particularly crucial for burn patients, where it focuses on hydration to ensure vital organ perfusion and manage shock. Additionally, fluid therapy plays an important role in managing diabetic ketoacidosis (cetoacidosis diab\u00e9tica). The practice is also commonly utilized in surgical contexts to support patients' hydration needs and overall stability during and after procedures."}{"title": "CRISTALOIDES:Cristaloides are a type of intravenous fluid used in medical treatment, particularly for hydration in conditions like cetoacidosis diab\u00e9tica."}{"title": "F\u00d3SFOROS:F\u00f3sforos are phosphates, which may be relevant in the context of electrolyte management in diabetic patients."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS L\u00c1CTICA:Acidosis l\u00e1ctica, or lactic acidosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lactic acid in the body. This condition can arise in various medical situations, including metabolic disturbances such as those seen in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0) and in individuals with Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes (MELAS). In GSD0, the diversion of excess glucose and intermediates towards lactic acid production can lead to this condition. In MELAS patients, lactic acidosis is a common occurrence resulting from mitochondrial dysfunction and is considered a diagnostic criterion for the syndrome. Additionally, lactic acidosis must be ruled out in children presenting symptoms before initiating a ketogenic diet, as it can indicate underlying metabolic issues. Overall, acidosis l\u00e1ctica is a significant metabolic disturbance that reflects a buildup of lactic acid in the body, often necessitating careful monitoring and management in affected individuals."}{"title": "RABDOMI\u00d3LISIS:Rabdomi\u00f3lisis, also known as rhabdomyolysis, is a serious medical condition characterized by the breakdown of muscle tissue. This condition can complicate the management of diabetes and may arise as a severe side effect of statin medications, which are commonly prescribed to lower cholesterol levels. The breakdown of muscle tissue in rabdomi\u00f3lisis can lead to significant health issues, including the risk of kidney failure."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME:S\u00edndrome refers to a group of symptoms that occur together, which can be relevant in the context of diabetes and its complications."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LITICA:Anal\u00edtica refers to laboratory tests and analyses that are crucial for diagnosing and managing diabetes and its complications.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "ENGL J MED:The New England Journal of Medicine, a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research and reviews in the field of medicine."}{"title": "CLEGG DJ:DJ Clegg is a medical professional who co-authored a paper on electrolyte and acid-base disturbances in patients with diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "ALLGROVE J:J Allgrove is a medical professional who contributed to the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "CRAIG ME:ME Craig is a medical professional who contributed to the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "EDGE J:J Edge is a medical professional who contributed to the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "GLASER N:N Glaser is a medical professional who contributed to the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "JAIN V:V Jain is a medical professional who contributed to the ISPAD Clinical Practice Consensus Guidelines on diabetic ketoacidosis and hyperglycemic hyperosmolar state."}{"title": "NEUROARTROPAT\u00cdA DE CHARCOT:A condition characterized by joint damage due to neuropathy, often associated with diabetes, requiring careful diagnosis and treatment."}{"title": "SEQUEIRA W:W Sequeira is a medical professional who authored a reference on the neuropathic joint."}{"title": "ARTROPAT\u00cdA NEUROP\u00c1TICA:A condition resulting from nerve damage that leads to joint damage, often seen in patients with diabetes."}{"title": "TOMOGRAF\u00cdA AXIAL COMPUTARIZADA:Tomograf\u00eda Axial Computarizada, also known as CT scan, is a diagnostic imaging technique utilized to create detailed images of internal organs, which is frequently employed in medical evaluations. This advanced imaging method allows for the identification of the location and causes of various medical conditions, including specific issues such as chylothorax."}{"title": "RADIOGRAF\u00cdA SIMPLE:A basic imaging technique used to visualize bones and certain body structures, commonly used in diagnosing joint issues."}{"title": "RESONANCIA MAGN\u00c9TICA NUCLEAR:An advanced imaging technique that uses magnetic fields and radio waves to create detailed images of organs and tissues in the body."}{"title": "GAMMAGRAF\u00cdA CON LEUCOCITOS MARCADOS:A diagnostic test that uses radioactive materials to visualize areas of infection or inflammation in the body."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA CORRECTORA CON ARTRODESIS:A surgical procedure aimed at correcting joint deformities through fusion of the bones."}{"title": "INMOVILIZACI\u00d3N CON DESCARGA TOTAL:A treatment approach that involves immobilizing a limb to relieve pressure and allow healing."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO CON ANTIBI\u00d3TICO PARENTERAL:A method of administering antibiotics directly into the bloodstream to treat severe infections."}{"title": "ADMINISTRACI\u00d3N DE BISFOSFONATOS:A treatment approach involving medications that help prevent bone loss and are sometimes used in joint conditions."}{"title": "TERAPIA F\u00cdSICA:A treatment method that uses physical methods, such as exercise and manipulation, to promote healing and improve mobility.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CHARCOT:Charcot refers to a condition related to diabetic neuropathy affecting the foot, leading to joint damage and deformity."}{"title": "EMPAGLIFLOZINA:Empagliflozina is a medication used to treat type 2 diabetes and has shown benefits in reducing cardiovascular events."}{"title": "LIRAGLUTIDA:Liraglutida is a GLP-1 analog and receptor agonist primarily used for the treatment of type 2 diabetes and obesity. It is recognized for its prolonged action, which enhances insulin release and helps manage blood sugar levels effectively. In addition to its primary role in diabetes management, Liraglutida has demonstrated cardiovascular benefits and is known to significantly reduce HbA1c levels. Furthermore, it promotes weight loss, making it an effective option for individuals seeking to manage both diabetes and obesity. Overall, Liraglutida is a multifaceted medication that addresses critical health concerns related to type 2 diabetes and weight management while also positively impacting cardiovascular risk markers."}{"title": "SEMAGLUTIDA:Semaglutida is another GLP-1 receptor agonist used for type 2 diabetes management, known for its cardiovascular benefits."}{"title": "TIAZOLIDINDIONA:Tiazolidindiona refers to a class of medications used to treat type 2 diabetes by improving insulin sensitivity."}{"title": "GLICLAZIDA:Gliclazida is a medication used to manage blood sugar levels in patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "ESTATINAS:Estatinas, also known as statins, are a class of medications primarily used to lower cholesterol levels in the blood. They are effective hypolipemiant drugs that help manage dyslipidemia, particularly by reducing LDL cholesterol levels. Estatinas are often prescribed to patients to mitigate cardiovascular risk, especially in individuals with conditions such as diabetes or chronic kidney disease, although their use may depend on the patient's overall health status.\n\nIn addition to their cholesterol-lowering effects, estatinas can also be utilized in the treatment of severe hypertriglyceridemia, although they are generally considered a second-line option due to their moderate impact on triglyceride levels. It is important to note that the effects of estatinas can be potentiated by alcohol consumption, which may influence their efficacy and safety profile.\n\nOverall, estatinas are widely recognized for their role in cardiovascular health and are a common choice in the management of lipid disorders."}{"title": "ANALITICA:An analytical test that includes lipid levels and HbA1c to assess diabetes management and cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "CUIDADO DIABETOL\u00d3GICO:Diabetological care involves education and management strategies for patients with diabetes to improve health outcomes."}{"title": "FCO. JAVIER SANTAMAR\u00cdA SANDI:Fco. Javier Santamar\u00eda Sandi is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, currently working at the Hospital Universitario Cruces and an associate professor at the University of the Basque Country."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DEL PA\u00cdS VASCO:The Universidad del Pa\u00eds Vasco, also known as the University of the Basque Country, is a prominent educational institution in Spain. It is notable for being the alma mater of Francisco Javier Escalada San Mart\u00edn, who graduated in Medicine in 1986. Additionally, the university employs Fco. Javier Santamar\u00eda Sandi as an associate professor in the Department of Medicine, contributing to its academic reputation in the field of medical education."}{"title": "SEDYNE:The Sociedad de Endocrinolog\u00eda, Diabetes y Nutrici\u00f3n de Euskadi (SEDyNE) is a professional society that Fco. Javier Santamar\u00eda Sandi presided over from March 2011 to March 2016."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE TIROIDES:C\u00e1ncer de tiroides, or thyroid cancer, is a condition characterized by the abnormal growth of cells in the thyroid gland. This type of cancer has been associated with obesity, although the exact mechanisms remain unclear. Treatment for thyroid cancer may involve specific therapies, such as radioiodine therapy. \n\nResearch has suggested that there is no significant association between the consumption of fish and the development of thyroid cancer. However, the relationship between thyroid cancer and the intake of fruits and vegetables is more controversial, particularly due to the presence of thiocyanates in cruciferous vegetables, which may influence thyroid health.\n\nAdditionally, thyroid cancer can be a potential complication for patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), although the connection between thyroid cancer and the MEN1 gene is not well established. \n\nThe Thyroid Cancer Working Group, a committee within the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition, has been involved in addressing issues related to thyroid cancer, with Fco. Javier Santamar\u00eda Sandi serving as secretary from 2012 to 2016."}{"title": "HIPOTIROIDISMO:HIPOTIROIDISMO, or hypothyroidism, is a medical condition characterized by the insufficient production of thyroid hormones by the thyroid gland. This deficiency leads to a slow metabolism and can result in various health problems, including decreased energy levels. Additionally, hypothyroidism may contribute to low levels of copper in the body and can influence sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels, which in turn affects testosterone levels. It is also noted that hypothyroidism can be a common adverse effect associated with certain immune checkpoint inhibitors, such as ipilimumab and nivolumab. The condition encompasses various forms, including congenital hypothyroidism, which has specific implications for affected individuals. Overall, hypothyroidism is a significant health concern that impacts metabolic function and hormonal balance."}{"title": "ROSIGLITAZONA:Rosiglitazone is a medication that has shown to improve \u03b2-cell function and insulin sensitivity in patients with type 2 diabetes, as highlighted in the ADOPT study."}{"title": "METFORMINA:Metformina, or metformin, is a medication primarily used for the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus. It works by improving insulin sensitivity, which helps manage blood sugar levels in patients with this condition. However, in some cases, such as when a patient has low glomerular filtration rates, metformin may be suspended due to potential risks. Additionally, it is recommended that metformin be withdrawn two days prior to any studies if gastrointestinal tumors are suspected.\n\nWhile metformin is effective in managing diabetes, it can be associated with side effects, including diarrhea and a reduction in vitamin B12 concentrations. In clinical studies, such as the ADOPT study, metformin has been compared to other medications like rosiglitazone, particularly in terms of glycemic durability. Overall, metformin remains a widely used and important medication in the management of type 2 diabetes, although careful consideration of patient-specific factors is necessary for its use."}{"title": "GLIBURIDA:Gliburide is another alternative medication for type 2 diabetes that is compared to rosiglitazone in the ADOPT study."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS:ANTICUERPOS are proteins produced by the immune system in response to various stimuli, including allergens and specific proteins such as gluten in individuals with celiac disease. They play a crucial role in the immune response, with different types of antibodies serving distinct functions. For instance, antibodies against the thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) receptor can be present in newborns with congenital hypothyroidism, affecting thyroid function. Additionally, antibodies such as IgE are produced in response to allergens, contributing to allergic reactions. Furthermore, these antibodies are utilized in diagnostic tests for conditions like celiac disease, highlighting their importance in both immune response and medical diagnostics."}{"title": "CRIBADO NEONATAL:Neonatal screening is a process that helps identify congenital hypothyroidism in newborns, with varying incidence rates depending on the country and screening practices."}{"title": "DISGENESIA TIROIDEA:Disgenesia tiroidea, also known as thyroid dysgenesis, is recognized as the primary cause of congenital hypothyroidism, accounting for approximately 85% of cases. This condition plays a significant role in the overall incidence of congenital hypothyroidism, highlighting its importance in the field of endocrinology and pediatric health."}{"title": "QUEBEC:Quebec is a province in Canada where a 20-year retrospective population-based study on congenital hypothyroidism was conducted."}{"title": "DELADOEY J:Deladoey J is one of the authors of the study on the incidence of congenital hypothyroidism in Quebec."}{"title": "RUEL J:Ruel J is one of the authors of the study on the incidence of congenital hypothyroidism in Quebec."}{"title": "GIGUERE Y:Giguere Y is one of the authors of the study on the incidence of congenital hypothyroidism in Quebec."}{"title": "VAN VLIET G:Van Vliet G is an author recognized for contributions to the field of paediatric endocrinology, particularly in relation to congenital hypothyroidism. They are one of the authors of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism, which provides important recommendations and standards for the diagnosis and management of this condition. Additionally, Van Vliet G has co-authored a study examining the incidence of congenital hypothyroidism in Quebec, further contributing to the understanding and research surrounding this endocrine disorder."}{"title": "J CLIN ENDOCRINOL METAB:The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism (J Clin Endocrinol Metab) is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research and clinical practice guidelines related to endocrinology and metabolism. It features a wide range of studies, including those focused on adrenal insufficiency, hyponatremia, congenital hypothyroidism, thyroid disease, and conditions such as pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma. The journal has also published significant clinical practice guidelines on endocrine treatment for gender-dysphoric individuals, as well as research on the syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIAD) and glucocorticoid deficiency. Overall, J Clin Endocrinol Metab serves as a vital resource for advancements in the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "LAFRANCHI SH:LaFranchi SH is an author recognized for contributions to the field of neonatal health, specifically focusing on the diagnosis and treatment of neonatal hypothyroidism. Their work includes significant studies that explore various aspects of this condition, providing valuable insights into effective management and therapeutic approaches."}{"title": "LEGERS J:Leger J is an author of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "HORM RES PEDIATR:Horm Res Pediatr is the journal where the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines were published."}{"title": "RODRIGUEZ A:Rodr\u00edguez A is an author who wrote about neonatal screening in endocrine diseases."}{"title": "REV ESP ENDOCRINOL PEDIATR:Rev Esp Endocrinol Pediatr is the journal where the article on neonatal screening in endocrine diseases was published."}{"title": "DEFECTOS EN LA S\u00cdNTESIS DE HORMONAS TIROIDEAS:Defects in the synthesis of thyroid hormones are the second most common cause of congenital hypothyroidism, explaining 10% to 15% of cases."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS BLOQUEANTES DEL RECEPTOR DE LA TSH:Maternal transfer of blocking antibodies to the TSH receptor can cause transient congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "LITIO:LITIO, or lithium, is a medication primarily used as a mood stabilizer in the treatment of mood disorders. It is known to affect various physiological processes in the body. One significant effect of lithium is its potential to alter calcium levels, leading to conditions such as hypercalcemia. Additionally, the excretion of lithium is influenced by sodium intake, which can impact its effectiveness and safety.\n\nLithium is also associated with several side effects, including the development of primary hypothyroidism in up to 20% of patients undergoing treatment. Another notable side effect is nephrogenic diabetes insipidus, which can occur in some individuals taking the medication. Overall, while lithium is an effective treatment for mood disorders, it requires careful monitoring due to its various effects on the body and potential side effects."}{"title": "AMIODARONA:Amiodarona is an antiarrhythmic medication that is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. This drug is notable for its high iodine content, which can lead to thyroid dysfunction in approximately 15-20% of patients. Specifically, amiodarona can induce both hyperthyroidism and hypothyroidism, particularly in individuals with pre-existing thyroiditis. The risk of hypothyroidism is especially pronounced in regions where there is a low intake of iodine. Overall, amiodarona is a significant medication in the management of arrhythmias, but it carries the potential for thyroid-related side effects that require monitoring."}{"title": "INTERFER\u00d3N \u0391:Interfer\u00f3n \u03b1 is a medication known for its antiviral and antineoplastic properties. It is utilized in the treatment of various conditions, including hepatitis C, leukemias, mastocytosis, carcinoid syndrome, and Beh\u00e7et's disease. However, it can also lead to thyroid dysfunction, manifesting as both hyperthyroidism and hypothyroidism. Additionally, Interfer\u00f3n \u03b1 may induce autoimmune thyroid diseases, such as Hashimoto's thyroiditis."}{"title": "LIU YY:Liu YY is an author who contributed to research on thyroid hormone interactions and metabolic regulation."}{"title": "BRENT GA:Brent GA is a notable figure in the field of endocrinology, particularly recognized for his contributions to thyroid health. He is a co-author of the 2017 Guidelines of the American Thyroid Association for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Disease During Pregnancy and the Postpartum, which underscores his expertise in this critical area of healthcare. Additionally, Brent GA is known for his research on thyroid hormone signaling and its effects on metabolism, further highlighting his significant role in advancing the understanding of thyroid function and its implications for overall health."}{"title": "MARATOU E:Maratou E is an author who studied insulin resistance in patients with hypothyroidism."}{"title": "HADJIDAKIS DJ:Hadjidakis DJ is an author involved in research related to thyroid function and metabolic disorders."}{"title": "KOLLIA A:Kollia A is an author who has contributed to studies on thyroid dysfunction and its effects on lipid profiles."}{"title": "RIZOS CV:Rizos CV is an author who researched the effects of thyroid dysfunction on cardiovascular health."}{"title": "ELISAF MS:Elisaf MS is an author known for his work on the lipid profiles in thyroid dysfunction."}{"title": "LIBEROPOULOS EN:Liberopoulos EN is an author who studied the impact of thyroid disorders on lipid metabolism."}{"title": "SILVA JE:Silva JE is an author who researched thyroid-adrenergic interactions and their clinical implications."}{"title": "WIERSINGA WM:Wiersinga WM is an author who has written extensively on adult hypothyroidism."}{"title": "ENDOTEXT:Endotext is a comprehensive online resource for endocrinology, providing information on various endocrine disorders, including hypothyroidism."}{"title": "T3:T3, or triiodothyronine, is a crucial thyroid hormone that plays a significant role in regulating metabolism and energy levels in the body. It is the more active form of thyroid hormone, derived from T4 (thyroxine) in target cells. T3 is particularly important for metabolic processes and is typically found at low levels in patients with Anorexia Nervosa, indicating its relevance in energy regulation and overall metabolic health."}{"title": "T4:T4, also known as thyroxine, is a crucial thyroid hormone produced by the thyroid gland. It plays a significant role in regulating metabolism and is essential for normal growth and metabolic processes. T4 levels are often measured in thyroid function tests to assess thyroid health. In certain conditions, such as Anorexia Nervosa, T4 can be found at low-normal levels due to malnutrition, indicating a potential disruption in metabolic regulation. Additionally, T4 is converted into its active form, T3, in target cells, which is necessary for exerting its metabolic effects."}{"title": "T3 REVERSA:Reverse T3 (rT3) is an inactive form of T3 that can increase in certain conditions, such as severe illness or hypothyroidism."}{"title": "ADRENALINA:ADRENALINA, also known as adrenaline, is a hormone produced by the adrenal glands that plays a crucial role in the body's response to stress. It increases heart rate and enhances energy availability, which can be particularly important in emergency situations. The response to adrenaline can be affected by conditions such as hypothyroidism. Additionally, adrenaline is utilized as an emergency treatment for severe anaphylactic reactions, especially in patients with food allergies. It is essential for patients at risk of severe allergic reactions to have this medication readily available for self-administration in case of an emergency."}{"title": "AMPC:AMPC, or cyclic AMP (adenosine monophosphate cyclic), is a crucial secondary messenger involved in various biological processes. It plays a significant role in cellular signaling pathways, particularly those influenced by thyroid hormones. Additionally, AMPC is affected by the Gs\u03b1 protein, which is integral to its function in cellular signaling. This highlights the importance of AMPC in mediating responses within the cell and its involvement in complex regulatory mechanisms."}{"title": "DESYODASAS:Deiodinases are enzymes that convert thyroid hormones into their active or inactive forms, playing a key role in thyroid hormone metabolism."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD GRAVE:Severe illness can lead to changes in thyroid function, affecting hormone levels and metabolism.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "HEMANGIOMAS:Los hemangiomas son tumores vasculares que pueden estar asociados con hipotiroidismo debido a la expresi\u00f3n elevada de la enzima yodotironina desyodasa tipo 3, que afecta la producci\u00f3n de hormonas tiroideas."}{"title": "TIROIDITIS DE HASHIMOTO:La tiroiditis de Hashimoto es una enfermedad autoinmune que afecta la tiroides, caracterizada por la inflamaci\u00f3n de esta gl\u00e1ndula. Esta condici\u00f3n a menudo se asocia con el uso de interfer\u00f3n \u03b1, que puede inducir su aparici\u00f3n. La tiroiditis de Hashimoto se manifiesta frecuentemente con la presencia de bocio y niveles elevados de anticuerpos antitiroideos, lo que indica una respuesta inmune anormal contra el tejido tiroideo."}{"title": "LEVOTIROXINA:Levotiroxina is a medication that serves as a synthetic form of the thyroid hormone, primarily utilized in the treatment of hypothyroidism. It is particularly important in managing congenital hypothyroidism, where it acts as the primary treatment option. However, the absorption of levotiroxina can be influenced by other medications, such as carbamazepine, which may affect its efficacy."}{"title": "DAVIES TF:Davies TF is an author recognized for his contributions to the literature on the physiology and diagnosis of thyroid disorders. He has also played a significant role in the field of endocrinology, specifically discussing hyperthyroid disorders in a textbook on the subject. His work encompasses both theoretical and practical aspects of thyroid function, making him a notable figure in the study of endocrine health."}{"title": "SCHLUMBERGER M:Schlumberger M es un autor que ha escrito sobre la fisiolog\u00eda tiroidea y su evaluaci\u00f3n diagn\u00f3stica."}{"title": "HAY ID:Hay ID es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la fisiolog\u00eda y diagn\u00f3stico de trastornos tiroideos."}{"title": "WILLIAMS:Williams es la editorial del \"Textbook of Endocrinology\", que incluye informaci\u00f3n sobre la fisiolog\u00eda y diagn\u00f3stico de trastornos tiroideos."}{"title": "CAP\u00cdTULO 11:El cap\u00edtulo 11 del \"Textbook of Endocrinology\" se centra en la fisiolog\u00eda tiroidea y la evaluaci\u00f3n diagn\u00f3stica de trastornos tiroideos."}{"title": "CAP\u00cdTULO 12:El cap\u00edtulo 12 del \"Textbook of Endocrinology\" tambi\u00e9n aborda temas relacionados con la fisiolog\u00eda y diagn\u00f3stico de trastornos tiroideos."}{"title": "TIROIDES 3:TIROIDES 3 is a topic associated with hypothyroidism and its diagnosis, often referenced in the context of inquiries regarding this condition. Additionally, TIROIDES 3 pertains to a section or table that classifies responses in differentiated thyroid cancer, offering detailed descriptions of various response categories. This dual focus highlights TIROIDES 3's relevance in both the diagnosis of hypothyroidism and the evaluation of responses in thyroid cancer cases."}{"title": "SALVATORE D:"}{"title": "GU\u00cdA ATA 2014:The American Thyroid Association's 2014 guidelines recommend specific practices for the management of thyroid hormone absorption and treatment in patients with thyroid disorders."}{"title": "CISTINOSIS:Cystinosis is a rare autosomal recessive lysosomal storage disease characterized by the accumulation of cystine crystals, primarily affecting the kidneys and thyroid."}{"title": "HORMONA TIROIDEA:HORMONA TIROIDEA, or thyroid hormone, is produced with the assistance of iodine and plays a crucial role in metabolic processes and development in humans. The primary thyroid hormones, T4 (thyroxine) and T3 (triiodothyronine), are essential for regulating metabolism. Their production and function can be influenced by various factors, including pH levels and interactions with medications."}{"title": "YEYUNO:The yeyuno is the second part of the small intestine, playing a crucial role in the digestive process. It is primarily responsible for the absorption of most nutrients from digested food, including calcium. Additionally, the yeyuno is significant for the absorption of medications, which occurs through passive diffusion or transport proteins."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR PAEDIATRIC ENDOCRINOLOGY:The European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology (ESPE) is an organization that provides guidelines for the treatment of congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "HIPOTIROIDISMO CONG\u00c9NITO:Congenital hypothyroidism is a medical condition that requires early treatment to ensure normal neurological development in affected infants."}{"title": "DIMITROPOULOS A:Dimitropoulos A is an author of a study on long-term intellectual outcomes in children with congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "MOLINARI L:Molinari L is an author of a study on long-term intellectual outcomes in children with congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "ETTER K:Etter K is an author of a study on long-term intellectual outcomes in children with congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "TORRESANI T:Torresani T is an author recognized for contributions to the field of pediatric endocrinology, particularly in relation to congenital hypothyroidism. They have authored a study focusing on the long-term intellectual outcomes in children affected by this condition. Additionally, Torresani T is also a contributor to the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism, further emphasizing their expertise and involvement in establishing best practices for the management of this disorder."}{"title": "LANG-MURITANO M:Lang-Muritano M is an author of a study on long-term intellectual outcomes in children with congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "JENNI OG:Jenni OG is an author of a study on long-term intellectual outcomes in children with congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "GRASBERGER H:Grasberger H is an author of a study on genetic causes of congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "REFETOFF S:Refetoff S is a prominent researcher recognized for significant contributions to the understanding of thyroid hormone action and related disorders. He has played a crucial role in the classification of inherited defects of thyroid hormone action, enhancing the scientific community's knowledge in this area. Additionally, Refetoff S is the author of a study that explores the genetic causes of congenital hypothyroidism, further underscoring his expertise and impact in the field of thyroid research."}{"title": "GROZINSKY-GLASBERG S:Grozinsky-Glasberg S is an author of a meta-analysis on thyroxine-triiodothyronine combination therapy versus thyroxine monotherapy."}{"title": "FRASER A:Fraser A is an author of a meta-analysis on thyroxine-triiodothyronine combination therapy versus thyroxine monotherapy."}{"title": "NAHSHONI E:Nahshoni E is an author of a meta-analysis on thyroxine-triiodothyronine combination therapy versus thyroxine monotherapy."}{"title": "WEIZMAN A:Weizman A is an author of a meta-analysis on thyroxine-triiodothyronine combination therapy versus thyroxine monotherapy."}{"title": "LEIBOVICI L:Leibovici L is an author of a meta-analysis on thyroxine-triiodothyronine combination therapy versus thyroxine monotherapy."}{"title": "LEGER J:Leger J is an author of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "OLIVIERI A:Olivieri A is an author of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "DONALDSON M:Donaldson M is an author of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "KRUDE H:Krude H is an author of the European Society for Paediatric Endocrinology Consensus Guidelines on congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "DONALDSON M<(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS ANTILEVOTIROXINA:Anticuerpos antilevotiroxina are antibodies that may be present in patients with certain thyroid disorders, including Graves' disease."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE GRAVES:Graves' disease, known as \"enfermedad de Graves\" in Spanish, is an autoimmune disorder that leads to hyperactivity of the thyroid gland, resulting in hyperthyroidism. This condition is characterized by the presence of antibodies that bind to the thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) receptor, which stimulates the thyroid gland's overproduction of hormones. Graves' disease can also be associated with other autoimmune disorders and may lead to complications such as hypoparathyroidism and goiter. Overall, it is a significant health condition that affects the endocrine system and requires careful management."}{"title": "TAQUICARDIA SINUSAL:Taquicardia sinusal is a common cardiovascular manifestation associated with hyperthyroidism, including in patients with Graves' disease."}{"title": "MEDICINA NUCLEAR:Medicina nuclear refers to a medical specialty that uses radioactive substances for diagnosis and treatment, often used in evaluating thyroid function."}{"title": "DESHALOGENAS:Deshalogenas are enzymes involved in the metabolism of thyroid hormones, and defects in these enzymes can lead to congenital hypothyroidism."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA TRANSPORTADORA DE YODO NIS:La prote\u00edna transportadora de yodo NIS (Na/I symporter) is essential for iodine uptake in the thyroid gland, and its dysfunction can lead to thyroid disorders."}{"title": "MIXEDEMA PRETIBIAL:El mixedema pretibial es una manifestaci\u00f3n cl\u00ednica infrecuente de la enfermedad de Graves, con una prevalencia de alrededor del 5%."}{"title": "ESTR\u00c9S:ESTR\u00c9S, aunque ha sido relacionado con la aparici\u00f3n de la enfermedad de Graves, carece de evidencias s\u00f3lidas que respalden esta conexi\u00f3n. Adem\u00e1s, el estr\u00e9s se manifiesta como una respuesta fisiol\u00f3gica que puede aumentar los requerimientos nutricionales y afectar la recuperaci\u00f3n despu\u00e9s de una cirug\u00eda."}{"title": "FIBRILACI\u00d3N AURICULAR:Fibrilaci\u00f3n auricular, or atrial fibrillation, is a heart condition characterized by an irregular and often rapid heart rate. This condition was present in the patient and significantly contributed to his risk of stroke. Atrial fibrillation is classified as a type of cardiac arrhythmia, which can be influenced by various factors, including obesity. Additionally, there is some evidence suggesting that the use of fish oil may help manage atrial fibrillation, although further research is needed to confirm these potential benefits. Furthermore, atrial fibrillation can also be a cardiovascular complication associated with hyperthyroidism, particularly in individuals over the age of 60."}{"title": "BOELAERT K:Boelaert K is a notable author involved in significant research and guidelines related to thyroid health. He has contributed to a study focusing on hyperthyroidism in older individuals, highlighting the importance of understanding this condition in the aging population. Additionally, Boelaert K is an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer, which were published in the journal Clinical Endocrinology. This work underscores his expertise and influence in the field of endocrinology, particularly concerning thyroid disorders."}{"title": "BRIX TH:Brix TH es uno de los autores de un estudio que relaciona el tabaquismo con la enfermedad tiroidea autoinmune."}{"title": "KLEIN I:Klein I es uno de los autores que ha investigado la relaci\u00f3n entre la enfermedad tiroidea y el coraz\u00f3n."}{"title": "SMITH TJ:Smith TJ es un autor que ha escrito sobre la enfermedad de Graves."}{"title": "RECEPTOR DE TSH:El receptor de TSH es una prote\u00edna en la superficie de las c\u00e9lulas tiroideas que se une a la hormona estimulante de la tiroides, siendo un objetivo de los anticuerpos en la enfermedad de Graves."}>s1␀␀␀␀␀v1␀␀␀␀␀µv1␀␀␀␀␀Êz1␀␀␀␀␀≥|1␀␀␀␀␀w~1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀gÄ1␀␀␀␀␀Å1␀␀␀␀␀WÇ1␀␀␀␀␀ŒÉ1␀␀␀␀␀¬Ñ1␀␀␀␀␀∆Ö1␀␀␀␀␀ùà1␀␀␀␀␀Xâ1␀␀␀␀␀'ä1␀␀␀␀␀Úä1␀␀␀␀␀yå1␀␀␀␀␀´ê1␀␀␀␀␀bë1␀␀␀␀␀˘ë1␀␀␀␀␀òí1␀␀␀␀␀<ì1␀␀␀␀␀î1␀␀␀␀␀≈ó1␀␀␀␀␀Rò1␀␀␀␀␀¿ò1␀␀␀␀␀Jô1␀␀␀␀␀∏õ1␀␀␀␀␀ú1␀␀␀␀␀ˆû1␀␀␀␀␀¢ü1␀␀␀␀␀g¢1␀␀␀␀␀˜¢1␀␀␀␀␀£1␀␀␀␀␀¸£1␀␀␀␀␀€§1␀␀␀␀␀ß1␀␀␀␀␀®ß1␀␀␀␀␀L®